    20	## Where we enter
    21	
    22	It is later on the hundred and thirty-first morning, at Lowmarch's lower inn hearth, after Oryn's letter and Karis's "Someone made this pattern." The first snow fell on day 129. The last ferry crossed and its lines were taken in on day 130; the ferryman is not taking ropes in now. A hand's depth of snow lies on the road. There are five at the lower inn. Lira's left arm is slung high and holds nothing; her right ankle is taped and unmended; she has Oryn's crossbow, hook and one bolt. Brom's shoulder is mended twice and held in four yards of webbing. Karis, Ember Iron Rank Three, has 52 sheets, the dead man's ledger, the four-circle map and Ternhall brass. Seln has his locked case, shut. Cael is nineteen, with ten fragments, 27 deployments behind him, and a still place untouched by order. Hesk's brass is in his coat. The living purse is 96 marks; the sealed reserve is separate. The brown mule is with the five. Teague's five are at the upper inn. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 18]
    23	
    24	## What this movement is for
    25	
    26	Put the cold term on the page [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19] and teach hard. This is the first third, so the formula wants progression vocabulary at its densest here. The reader should finish the movement knowing all ten fragments as costs and limits, and the kit as a tool. They should know that instruments read wrong in one pair of hands, and why Karis cannot let go of the index. The movement ends with six at a table and a word nobody has said yet: west.
    27	
    28	Consequential turns and promises:
    29	- **The cold stay priced** (133rd): Pike's four a month; "Eleventh"; seventy-six left. Then the cold-term board [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19]: a roof, a well-house, a fence.
    30	- **The fence at the axe-head hold** (~140th, ~3,000 for the set piece). This is two days out on the cold road. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19] A shale-back herd shelters on the fence line's slope and must be moved without stampeding, with no Path that matters. Lira is benched in her sling and reads the herd for them. Brom reads the line of posts like a wall. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. The factor pays forty at the gate and asks no name: 116, and the tenth line, PAID.
    31	- **The ice road** (161st, ~3,000). A carter's cart goes through the river ice. Cael, Brom and Seln haul it out without declaring. Cael's Iron read on the ice's load is the workhorse, taught as a practical skill.
    32	- **The silent yard** (two or three bouts across the cold term, ~1,500 each) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19]. Teague's crew and the five spar in the frozen meadow with steel and bodies, and no Paths. Cael loses to the tall woman's spear reach, then makes a visible correction. She never says a word to any of the five. Lira coaches from the bench, one-armed. The rival clock appears on the page. Teague is the better field captain.
    33	- **Cael's working inventory** (~6,000, across private practice in the ferryman's shed or the meadow at night). Each of the ten has its cost: Wind's burst and the lock beat; Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" when spoken); the Iron read; Compression's frame; Ember, one point at a time, with its burn (used at the Ring and the Stair); [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] Shadow's idle draw and the seal; Storm, its lanes and their bills (ten / ten / twelve; four lanes laid in Book 7; untested past three in a row); [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] Anchor used both ways; Blade; Tide, self and contact, which he has run on himself three times; no outward use without an ask and explicit yes. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19]
    34	- **The anomaly as a scene** (168th). Karis has everyone pace the yard with the cord. It reads forty-two for everyone and "forty-one and a piece" for him, three times. The edges read a hair short and a hair long in his hands. Her ruler sentence is said twice, first as a rule and then not as one. Log it verbatim: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
    35	- **Karis's case grows in pieces** through the cold term. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19] She says the full sentence about west on the 263rd. The thaw comes, and the Thornwater road opens on the 264th.
    36	- **Thornwater** (265th–266th). The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. "Five months and twenty days." [OWNER-pending #56] / "That's a season. Take it off." Oryn waits for Lira to undo the sling herself. "Will you mend it." / "Lie still": this is Lira's first ask since Norhold. The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole." The map on her table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "Neither do you. Write that down too." She will not read him yet. She comes down to Lowmarch, unasked.
    37	- **Six at Lowmarch** (268th): 118 marks. Karis makes her case, and **Treswick and the Deepstacks are spoken for the first time**, along with the scholars' provision and "a man there who is". Oryn's reservation about the station goes unsaid. **The closing log (270th), verbatim.**
