     7	- Day 131, Lowmarch, later in the morning of Oryn's letter. Five at the lower inn (hearth's end for the standing-money; the store behind the chimney for the paper, six paid). Oryn at Thornwater, two days up a shut saddle. Teague's five at the upper inn for the cold term.
     8	- Cael: nineteen, no birthday in this book; no Path; his own Arbiter woke at his Kindling and went dark; ten fragments; **deployment since the Line twenty-seven**; Shadow used twice and sealed; Anchor used twice (once each way); Tide: himself three times, Oryn twice by her leave, nobody else; the still place left alone by order; ribs quiet since the 129th. Both brass edges read TRUE in his hand at entry.
     9	- Lira: left arm slung high, holds nothing until Oryn says; right ankle taped, unmended, in the carter's great boot; Oryn's crossbow, hook, one bolt. Brom: right shoulder in four yards of webbing; the knot is the older healer's. Karis: Iron Rank Three; fifty-two sheets (11/29/12); the kit and the dead man's ledger; the hide with four rings and a ruled line; the Ternhall brass; her hypothesis unsaid. Seln: the case shut.
    10	- Money: ninety-six in hand; the sealed reserve apart. Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman; a letter to Ephram. Pike: nine lines; the season line with no number; eleventh on the cloth.
    11	- Rules of the country: on roads and exposed fence-lines nobody declares; in the meadow and a steading's yard Paths are open. Shale-backs (Book 7): they do not answer fire, sound or a blow on their shelf; they answer fright in one of their own, all together, by moving away; "derived, not tested" for a declaration. The carters' rule: never be below them; never be loud below them.
