    15	1. **Teague's spear.** The packet and BOOK_MAP call this person "the tall woman". The edition's Book 7 says "a tall man" in Cael's point of view (ch52) and "He was not a man of many words" in Teague's (ch51). I give this person no pronoun and neither word: "the tall one", "Teague's spear" (Cael), "the spear" (Teague). The weapon in the yard is "the pole".
    16	2. **Whether Teague reads.** The plan says he does not read. Book 7 ch25 has him read a paper "from the first word to the seal". The packet's beat "he cannot read the sheet and does not need to" is staged as distance: Pike's cloth hangs in the lower inn and he is in the upper; he knows what it says.
