editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:176:**Vocabulary** (this series' own): fragment, notice, integration, acquisition (directed), engagement (clinical — non-hostile), Path, declaration, tier, rank, Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver/Gold, Arbiter, sigil, idle state, deployment, the hold, discharge, the reading (surface / deep), mending, reserve, the line, quiet ground → the Quieting, perimeter, radius, stake, the board, HOLD, outcome, the wall. The system's voices are the **log** (Cael's inventory), the **notice** (one only, the tenth), and **Pike's ledger lines**. Interface text appears only where the canon calls for it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:180:**How the first third teaches hard without spending anything:** the log's inventory of nine, with each fragment's idle rent named (Shadow at dusk, Anchor wanting doorways, Storm heavy); the discipline of holding as a skill with failure modes; the board's arithmetic (outcome, not tier); the carters' "don't declare"; the ford's discharge finding; the shale-backs' flight; Oryn's Tide taught in full (contact only, the reserve, three mendings a day, cannot heal herself, "cannot mend what I can't read," two readings); tier talk at the plank (Pike's Copper Force, Teague's unreported Bronze, Lira's Iron R1, Brom's Copper forever). **Cael deploys nothing in M1–M3 except the single ford burst.** The log reads "Deployment since the Line: one" from day 53 to day 90, and the edition keeps that count.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:192:| **Tide-adjacent (NEW, the tenth)** | M5 day 100 the deep reading; **the notice** (verbatim, §10); M6 cost: three days of *listening*, not pulling (his own current at the edge of thought; the nine audible as flows); the idle state learned by the third night; **the first self-reading** (a place near the middle that does not flow; location only; not named); M7 ask refused at the lean-to, granted on the road; the first reading of another person (Oryn: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things); M8 the second and third self-readings; **"the still place"** (the phrase appears first here); told to Oryn with his hand on her wrist; **Teague not read** | Contact only; surface at a count of ten, deep only with the subject still, whole and willing; does nothing in a fight; *ask first, every time*; "Things you keep touching don't heal" |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:193:| **The anomaly → the still place** | M1–M5: "Still open. Still real. Patience." M6: the three words retired, with the reason. M8: a location. **Not a fragment; never counted; not the Quiet** | No theory, name-as-explanation, or *before/source/primordial* |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:196:**Others' progression:** Lira learns to be fast with nothing at the end (M2), and learns to shoot braced one-armed (M6 → M8). Brom learns Iron Skin is a shout out here, and what he is without it ("a big man with good footwork and a lip of fused stone"). Karis learns to keep one point; the lattice line across a mountain; the wall along a line from her knees. Seln learns that his Path "was never most of what I do." Oryn: what her hands can and cannot do at a line, tested eight times alone. Teague: a column he does not have.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:207:| M1 | The cart out of the wash (rope, a far bank, three wheels) | 1,500 | Physical problem |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:240:Callbacks confirmed in Book 8's closed prose: Oryn's letter and "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." (B8 Ch1, Ch24); "a tape and a season" (B8 Ch1); "Lie still when I say" (B8 Ch18, Ch24); Brom's "Twice… not three times this season" (B8 Ch6); "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." (B8 Ch1, Ch5, Ch20); Hesk's "true to a hair" / "draw a line through it" / "Mind the shape" (B8 Ch1, Ch17, Ch18, Ch22, Ch24); "too small" (B8 Ch16, Ch17, Ch24); "Stop touching it." (B8 Ch7); "Not the Quiet." (B8 Ch7, Ch24); "He'll speak to you when you've cost him something" (B8 Ch7); Teague's after-thaw term [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] (B8 Ch1, Ch17); "Eleventh" (B8 Ch1, Ch12, Ch17); "the Bronze from Ardenmere" (B8 Ch7); ninety-six in hand (B8 Ch1); fifty-two sheets and forty-one kinds (B8 Ch9–11). Canon documents quote "Three points make a line. Four make an argument.", "Someone made this pattern.", the looms finding, "A circle is a made shape." and the stratum limit. Every other item below is a signature line or document of this book. **Keep them all exact.** Speaker attributions may be re-staged; the words may not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:264:- Ephram (Ch9), whole letter: *Cael — / Weather first, because you'll want it in order, and I've watched you want things in order. / The Crown yard has a new cohort captain. The intake came up the bluff a fortnight ago, forty-one of them, and they've put a third-year over them who was a second-year when you left and whose name you would not know, so I'll not spend the ink. He is fair. He counts slower than you did. They stand where he puts them. / Withrow's tenure holds. That is the whole of the sentence. I asked whether there was a longer one and was told there was not, in a way that meant there had been, for a week. / A query came down to the registry from somewhere above it. Bracken would not say where and I did not ask twice. It wanted former enrollees' last known direction of travel. Bracken answered it. He gave them a map reference to the Line and nothing past it — which is true, and which Bracken enjoyed being true. He told me so at the plaque wall with his hands behind his back, and then told me he had not told me. / I still lose to you every time I run it. I have stopped running it in the yard. / Rooke says the yard's quieter. He didn't say it was worse. He also didn't say it wasn't. / — E.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:265:- Vell (Ch9): *Filed with your record. It reads: left in good standing, undefeated on paper. I've kept this ledger forty years and never had a line like it. The session still stands. The road still runs through Ardenmere. — V.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:268:- Cael to Vell (Ch24): *Vell. There's a second ledger on the continent with my name in it, kept by a one-armed man in a town on no map, and this week he stopped numbering me. He said his book was wrong about us by being too small. You said once that somebody should have a record that doesn't answer to the Compact. There are two now. The session still stands. — C.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:277:- Ch7: *Teague priced us. He's right about the cart. Oryn read me three times and got nothing three times and wants a fourth. Two people out here measuring me, and neither of them has a seal. I keep waiting to mind.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:279:- Ch9, at the stone: *Quiet ground. Karis's Arbiter stopped at a line she can mark with a rock. So did Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's — same line, same step. Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen. I don't know what that means. Nobody asked. Tomorrow we go in.* [OWNER-pending #49]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:292:- Ch22, the still place: *Read myself. Ten currents, and I can't find the banks either — Oryn's right. And the anomaly's there. Not a fragment. Not a flow. A still place, and the rest of me has been going around it since before I knew it existed. It isn't the Quiet. The Quiet is outside me and turns Paths off. This is inside me and the Paths — the fragments — go around it like they were built to. I don't know what it is. I know it was there before Oryn, before Brom's read, before the ring. Session nine caught the edge of it. I'm not going to guess. Guessing is what the registry did to me. Observation, then the log, then patience.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:293:- Ch22, the stake paid: *Teague sat down next to me. Asked what I am. I could have read him. I asked instead. The day I stop asking is the day I'm the registry. Write it down. Again. Every time.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:294:- Ch23: *Hundred and twenty-second day, the fork. Oryn north. On her terms. I didn't ask. Five on the bearing.* — *I love this country.* — and the crest: *Four sites. One line. The last one's twice the size and the Compact fenced it. The bearing runs through it and keeps going. Karis says four points is an argument. I say it's a bearing — the kind their maps draw as nothing. Home is Lowmarch now. I just wrote that without noticing. Nineteen, ten fragments, a still place at the center of me, and a line on a map that somebody drew before there were maps. We're not done. We're oriented.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:295:- Ch24, the inventory: *Ten confirmed fragments.* / *Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — the Bronze from Ardenmere. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — Seln; source protected; the seal held past the Line as it held inside, and was used twice out here where no one who could carry it west could see it, and that is the seal's whole logic and it is unchanged. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; opened a door on a rim and held a floor in a hall, and I own a piece of the craft the system uses to hold people and have used it twice this year, once each way. Blade-adjacent — Ephram. Tide-adjacent — Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; the tenth, and the first that does nothing in a fight, and the only one whose engagement field says clinical, and the only one with a rule on it in her hand and mine: ask first, every time. Deployment notes current on all ten.* / *One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.* / *Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. Both are going to need a map.* — **Audio rule:** Feryn's name never appears in a list run beside Oryn's; every inventory says "the Bronze from Ardenmere."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:301:- Ch4: the carter's wife: "You mean the quiet ground? Everybody knows the quiet ground. Nobody goes in." — Lira: "So what am I becoming, exactly, if nobody's measuring?" — Seln: "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report." — Brom: "What does the board pay a man with no Path at all." / Pike: "Same as anyone," … "What'd he do?" — Pike: "Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something. That's not rudeness. That's the ledger."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:304:- Ch7: Oryn: "That's a tape and a season. It'll set." — "Twenty days," … "Round. Two at a hold, near enough, and the road between, and the road's the part that doesn't move." — "I remember who I've had my hands on," … "That's the book. A healer who needs a page to know who's owed has stopped looking at them." — "In the city I healed Bronzes with bruises. Out here I set legs. I'm not going back and I'm not stopping. The route is the only thing I own." — "It's like putting my hands in a river in the dark. Something's moving. I can't find the banks, so I can't read it, so I can't touch it. That's the rule. I didn't make it." — "When you're not broken, I run the long one. It won't read you either. I want to feel it not read you properly." — "Thornwater's on my route in nine days. You'll be on the board by then. Come find me. I want to read you when you're not broken." / "Nine days." — The ford-keeper: "Then they go round," … "That's worth seventy to know before the first cart's in the gorge. I'd sooner pay it for this." — Teague: "You cleared Thornwater's ford with five and lost a cart on the high bench with five." / "Yes." / "The ford was good work. The bench was a cart." … "The board's going to have you and me on the same contract inside a season. Be good enough that I'm glad."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:305:- Ch8: Pike: "Quiet ground's where the sigil goes to sleep. Yours. Everyone's. You walk a road, and there's a place on it where your Arbiter stops — not slows; stops — and you walk on past and it's back. There's a handful of them. Along the void roads, all of them. Carters walk round them, and have as long as there've been carters. The dogs live in them. Stillhounds. Nobody's asked them why. Why any of it, nobody knows and nobody's needed to, because the rule's *don't go in*, and the rule's never once failed anybody who kept it." … "That's what a carter knows. That's what I know. There's not a man on the ferry knows a word more." — "I've walked past the Fallow Ring two hundred times. Never once stepped over the line. Thirty years on the roads and I've never met a practitioner who did it twice." — Karis: "What's the line?" / Pike: "You'll know," he said. "Your Arbiter tells you. It stops." — Seln: "Somebody wrote this who learned to write inside."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:307:- Ch10: Karis: "Sixty-two cords and twenty strides," … "One thousand three hundred and seventy-four yards, and a piece." … "A circle is a made shape." — Lira: "like a clock that stopped and started again without losing the time." — Seln: "You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from." … "Five years in the weather. A cold term either side." — Brom: "Skin." — Karis: "It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend." — Seln: "I've a knife and fifteen years. It was never most of what I do." — Oryn: "Nothing. Not nothing in him. Nothing in my hands." … "A healer's hands stop working there." — Cael: "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." — Karis: "None I own. And I own more than the registry prints." — Seln: "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:308:- Ch11: Seln: "The road's cut." … "The grass. Where the cord went." — Oryn: "Move," … "I can't fix this here. Move." … "She keeps it." — **The order:** "A mend that deep holds nothing for a season. Nothing. That arm is not to hold. It's not to strike. It's not to catch. Not a rope, not a knife, not a fall, not a friend. Not until I say. And I'll say at first snow, near enough, if it's let alone." … "One arm. From here to the snow." — "The ankle's a tape and a season. I've told you that before." — Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes," Cael said. / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:310:- Ch13: Oryn: "You don't get a yes. You get told." — Karis: "Ephram fought you in earnest and the notice said non-hostile. This is earnest and it isn't a fight at all." … "The model doesn't say the engagement has to be a fight. It says it has to be real." — Seln: "That's not consent. It's the nearest thing to it the log's ever had, and it's still not it. I'd enter both." — Lira: "She asked to read you," … "She didn't ask for the rest. Those aren't the same sentence." — Oryn's twenty-minute report: "I can feel that there's movement. More than one. I can't count them — I can't find where one stops. There's no channel. Everyone has a channel; I feel the banks and I know the Path. I can't find the banks in you. I've looked for twenty minutes. It isn't that you're broken. It's that I can't find anything shaped like the thing I read." — "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something and not known what it was." — "Something just changed," she said. "In you. While I was in there." / "Yes." / "Did I do that?" / "No. I did." … "I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it. You've been still for twenty minutes. I want to see if you can manage twenty-one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:314:- Ch17: Pike: "Eleventh. Teague's ten up." … "I'd not take it." — Seln: "That's not a wage. That's a lure, cut to fit." … "This isn't a contract. It's a pre-restriction inventory. They've mapped what we do inside, and they've priced a floor where we can't do it." / Karis: "They don't know about Cael." / "They don't need to." … "They want the case. The boy's the price of the case." — "They'll send people. A lure's no use if nobody's waiting at the end of it. People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face." — Cael: "Inside the circle, I'm the only one who works. They chose a floor that makes the rest of you helpless. They don't know it doesn't do anything to me." — Brom: "Doors open both ways," … "I don't like it. I'm in." — Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away. I was right. We're going anyway." — Teague: "You're taking the Stair contract." / "Yes," Cael said. / "It's a bad contract." / "Yes." … "My crew's at Millrace in two days," Teague said. "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted." [OWNER-pending #50]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:315:- Ch18: Oryn: "No." … "You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next." — "You're asking me to break the route," / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." — "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." — **Terms:** "You're on the route now. Which means when I say lie still, you lie still, and when I say I can't help you, you believe me." — "Well?" / "May I read you?" / "Yes. That's the answer, and I'm the one giving it…" — "You're built to arrive." / "Yes," she said. "That's what I am." — Lira: "He asked twice and got one," / Brom: "That's the rate," — Seln: "Newer. This one's been re-surveyed."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:316:- Ch19: Brom: "Ridge," — Seln: "They can shoot the bowl," … "They can't shoot the stair." — Oryn: "I can see what's wrong. I can't feel it and I can't touch it. Tape it. Leave the bolt." … "the bolt's the plug" … "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." — Oryn: "Ask first," — Lira: "Later." / "Later." — Oryn at the stone: "There. Back," … "The clock started again." — "It held a stair. It's not going to hold anything else this season." — Seln: "No faces." — Teague: "You walked out of the Quiet declaring," / "Yes." … "Then you're not on the board anymore. You're something the board doesn't have a column for."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:317:- Ch20: Teague: "We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted" — Oryn: "What are they" / Karis: "Lines," — Karis: "He tried to drive it. Twice, by the head. It wouldn't go. Nothing goes into this." — Seln: "Nobody leaves a registry kit. It's signed out. You don't get another." … "I don't know what this is in, and I'm not going to say." — Karis: "Forty-one," … "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride, to the stride." … "The floor was carved by somebody who knew the circle's size," … "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:319:- Ch22: Oryn: "A still place that everything goes around. I've never felt that in anyone." / "Is it wrong?" / "I don't know what right would look like in you. Nobody does. That's not a comfort; it's a finding." … "Write it down and stop touching it. Things you keep touching don't heal." — Teague's healer: "Twice?" … "Then it wants binding, not hands," — Teague: "What are you." / Cael: "Why did you stop reporting?" / "Because the board pays the same whether I do or don't," … "and the registry doesn't, and I'd sooner be worth what I did than what they wrote." … "That's not an answer to mine." / "No." / "You didn't answer." / "I don't have one. Neither does the board. You said so." / "I did." … "The board's going to need a new column."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:320:- Ch23: Karis: "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." — "That's a healer's sentence," Oryn said … "I know whose it is," — Brom, Lira, Oryn at the first halt: "Twice," / "Twice," / "And not three," — Oryn at the fork: "I'm three weeks late there…" … "I've been a stop on my own route for nine days. I'm going back to being the route." … "Find me at Thornwater," … "Bring the map," — Karis: "Half the bend is twice the round. Four hundred. Near enough. Twice the radius. The same shape, at twice the size, round a thing I can't see." — Seln: "That's not a survey. That's a cordon. They've been here more than once." — Lira: "Twice the size. Is it twice the *anything else*?" — Cael: "Not without her. Not without knowing what a circle twice the size does to the four of you. And not without the map finished." / "It's finished," Karis said. "It's a line." / "Then it's a line that points somewhere. We go home and find out where."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:321:- Ch24: Pike: "Teague says you need a column I don't have. I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." — the carters: "Eleventh," / "Aye," — Teague: "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted," — Pike: "Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road," / Brom: "Ours," — Lira: "She'll say when," / Brom: "After the thaw," — *The sites were on an alignment. Not random.* — Karis: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) — **Closing, exact:** "I have ten things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no file I can see — and five people, one of them on a route, who've walked into the quiet three times and come out." He turned it over once and let it stand. "And a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." / Lira, one-armed, feeding the fire: "Then we follow it." / Brom: "After the thaw." / Karis, writing: "Noted." / Down the fire, the man who used to file reports about him watched the snow on the ferry landing with evident professional approval and said nothing, which — from him — was home. / Nothing out here had read him. At three floors older than any registry, every Path in the party had stopped at a line and his had not; a fourth had been paced from outside and not crossed. Nobody alive — least of all him — knew why. Someone had made the pattern. That was as far as anyone could say. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] [OWNER-pending #49]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:329:| Integration mechanism (revealed B3; sealed to the circle) | Oryn learns it on the 100th, told in full, the covenant page read; the circle becomes six | Tell Teague, Pike, any hold, the rim; let any cutaway outside the six guess it |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:335:| The still place | Located (M6, unnamed); named as *the still place* (M8); read three times; "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment." | *source, before, primordial, recurrence* (Book 9's word); a Rune-like "shape with bones" (Book 8's); any theory, including Oryn's |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:336:| The instruments reading wrong in his hands (B8 plant → B11) | Nothing | Any cord, stake or straightedge reading off in Cael's hand. **In Ch24 both edges touch for him as for Karis.** Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:337:| The Compact's six-year suppression / directive (B8) | Fieldwork only: stakes (31; 32 twice, one re-surveyed with the stroke-and-bar; 33; the 34 cordon), the maps' blanks, the kit and its ledger, a completion report going west | Policy, files, offices, the word "suppress," any date on the cordon, the stroke-and-bar or the index decoded |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:338:| The fourth site (B8's Sunken Span) | Paced from outside: about 190 paces to the line, twenty cords, half the bend, about 440 yards [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]; a standing grey shape taller than a man, neither ring nor stair; the cordon | Entering it; naming it; its effect on Arbiters; a watch-post; a sink, a bridge or piers seen clearly |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:342:| Teague's crew | Roles, small beats, the young one at the shafts | Any name (Book 8 says the young one's name once and does not enter it) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:351:- **C2 · The crew's mule.** From Ch16–17 the crew has "a mule" while Oryn has gone north "with … the mule's spare rope in her hand for the next hold's beast." At Millrace there are two mules; at the fork Oryn takes one and the crew keeps one, which stays in the ferryman's shed through the cold term (Book 8). [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; unlisted named-season hit found by the item-16 grep, same substitution as line 40] **Recommend:** stage Oryn's decision at Thornwater (day 110–111). She leaves her own mule with the crew for the boxes and a one-armed girl, and takes the route's beast at Millrace. An Oryn decision beat; no prose fact changes.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:352:- **C3 · Karis's measurements.** Ch23: "I've paced two and cord-measured the third." The Stair's perimeter was never paced on the page (Ch18: "I'll pace it in the morning", and the morning was the trap). At the Hall she stood "with the cord in her hand and not laid" (Ch21). **Recommend:** stage the Stair pacing on the morning of day 115 under Teague's rim watch, and the Hall's cord laid during the two marsh days (119–120). Ch23's sentence and the bible's "same radius at the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall" then become true on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:360:- **C11 · Small counts.** Ch17 has Pike turning the ledger "which he had done once before" (it was twice: Ch2, Ch8). Ch24 has "twice in a season" (it is the fourth). Ch22 has "no captain eleven lines up" when Teague is ten up at eleventh. The retelling counts honestly. Convention: "N up" counts positions above; "N between" counts lines between.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:368:**All canon names are kept**, including Bracken in Ephram's letter. **No new proper names are proposed.** The expansion is designed so that every new person is a role. **Do not name:** any member of Teague's crew (the spear, the bow with the limp, the young one, the older healer of no Path); the steading's woman and the bowman at Thornwater; the carters (the Thornwater carter, the carter's wife, the hide carter); the westbound courier at the ford; the ferryman and his boy; the smith and his boy; the landing broker and his clerk; the hide-woman; the crew of three and the mule-named crew on the wall; the ford-keepers at Oxhollow and Millrace; the miller; the old woman with the knee; the child three stops on; the four unnamed holds on Oryn's route; the six on the rim and the second Anchor specialist; the eleven-bale captain and the north-road woman captain. Site names stay descriptive (the Fallow Ring, the Long Stair, the Drowned Hall, **the fourth site**, unnamed). Fauna stay compound nouns (stillhound, shale-back, wold-wyrm).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:3:This is the entry state for this edition's Book 7. It is built from the CLOSED edition Book 6 prose, chapters 48–60, with the AFTER MOVEMENT 8 and AFTER MOVEMENT 9 coordinator rulings/CLOSED notes governing the handoff. **Append a dated section after each movement from the surviving prose.** Prose governs plans; coordinator rulings govern any recorded repair. Record plan deviations explicitly, and never overwrite canon silently. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A1]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:18:  - day 49: Lowmarch, the board, Teague seen
