editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:158:- **Ephram** at the academy above Ostrand. He stayed, and his absence is noted without grief. One letter in this book.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:182:- Cael: age; fragments (count, any change, deployment since the Line); injuries open; idle-state notes; the still place's status; money (earned / in hand).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:199:- **Deployment since the Line: none, through day 49** — the line counts CAEL'S fragments (said once in ch1). Companions' native Paths (Lira's involuntary burst, Brom's Iron Skin rising, Karis's point-lit fires) are not his deployments. Shadow's dusk drifts on days 5 and 24 are entered as "rent", not use. Anchor's one uncommanded doorway hold is Book 6 history, recalled once at Thornwater's ladder; Anchor remains undeployed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:201:- **Teague's healer is absent** (the packet's "no healer" governs; she joins later). Teague and Cael have not spoken. The Thornwater ford is unplaced; Movement 2 places it. The carter's light round trip (days 44–46) is an express-pace exception; the party's road stays two days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:206:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:228:- **Teague, as seen (flag):** forty or so, middle height, heavy in the forearm, cropped hair grey over the ears; a black leather band laced on the right wrist; a hand-axe in his belt; a coat mended by somebody else. His week on the cold road is salt on mules to the top holds before frost shuts the pass, along two miles of ledge; he has done it nine times. He thinks only "the spear", "the bow" (a bad leg), "the boy". One other crew on the sheet could clear the ford and is up the north road.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:236:**Where everyone is.** All five at one table in the lower inn, under the wall, with one jug. They sleep in the meadow. Teague and his three are on the sill of the same room and go out on the cold road at first light on day 50 for a week.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:238:**Cael.** Eighteen, said to Pike on day 9. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly** (*Still open. Still real. Patience.*, written on day 18). **Deployment since the Line: none.** No injury; the forearm is "sound again" by day 5 and is not mentioned afterward. Idle states: Shadow sealed, costing from waking, drifting at dusk (two drifts, logged as rent); Anchor asking at every sill, gate, rim and rail; Blade asking *Edge?* and taking names; Storm heavy; Wind leaning his feet. He has not read the Iron read once. The log has an entry for most days, each ending on the deployment line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:244:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Uninjured. Sets no points on a road. Holds: the field archive; a leaf headed *stillhound*, underlined once, with five counts and *110 yards* (*gate to stone; C.'s count, paced at a yard to the stride; not taped*); the entry of her own not-asking (day 22); the five column heads with *Outcome* underlined twice; Pike's copied line; **the carter's map**. She has asked nobody what the animal is waiting for.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:250:**Pike's book and the wall.** A heading of five names; **four lines**: *Ferry, the landing's goods. Six crossings stood. Nothing lost. Two marks.* (day 14); the fence (forty posts cut and set; four marks and flour; the saying is not on the page); the wash (three marks; not on the page); and the protected Thornwater line (day 49). **Thirteenth of thirteen; eleven lines between theirs and the top.** The top line is *Teague.* On the plank: *Thornwater ford. Clearance. Forty marks.* with *HOLD. Teague.* in Pike's capitals.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:252:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. Pike has not asked what Cael is, and has said that he never asked. Three people have called him paper and been told yes. The party knows the word *stillhound* and nothing of what it hunts by, or by what sense it followed a buckle; it has Cael's five counts, Seln's unshared reading of the ground, and the country's rule without its reason. **Nobody has heard the words "quiet ground".** Teague has read the five and found Seln on his second pass; he cannot tell what Cael is. Cael has read Teague. They have not spoken.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:260:- **The companions have failed before succeeding at the hold:** Lira has one involuntary practice burst, Brom has let Iron Skin rise and put it down, and Karis has lit at ninety and later held unlit to three hundred. These are native-Path events, not additions to Cael's deployment count (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:21-65`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:7`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:266:- **Board texture at handoff:** four earned lines, thirteenth of thirteen with eleven between them and Teague, Thornwater's ford held under Teague's name, and Pike's plank physically crowded but not count-fixed (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:103-123,181-227,271-277`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:267:- **Teague's day-49 read:** he counts only spear, bow and boy; the bow has a bad leg; he knows the Thornwater road and considers its ford worse than the stretch; he finds Seln on the second pass and cannot tell what Cael is. He and Cael have not spoken (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:299-353,359-379`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:277:- **Deployment since the Line: ONE** — a single Wind burst at the ford on day 53. None before; none after. Shadow is unused by Cael and stays sealed. Seln's use of his OWN native Shadow Path under water at the ford is not Cael's deployment and stands (it tested the water clause).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:281:- **Teague is absent:** back on the 57th and out again, known only by Pike's report. No meeting.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:286:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:306:- **Teague:** back down the cold road on the 57th; read the struck slip twice and the five's line; took two holds' slips from the north end of the plank and went up the north water at next light. Not seen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:315:**Where everyone is.** All five at Lowmarch, sleeping in the meadow, with the three boxes in the loft over the ferryman's drum. Teague and his three are out on two holds' slips up the north water.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:317:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (a single Wind burst at the ford on day 53, in front of the hold's bowman). Shadow unused; it lifted at dusk through the wait at the ford and again on the walk down the bar and was refused. Ember offered a point in the hound's mouth over Karis and was refused. The Iron read stays shut. Left calf bitten through on day 53: a leg on level ground, nine strides uphill. He has not asked Seln for his report, has not answered Lira's question, has not answered Hesk's letter, and has stopped counting Lira's runs. He knows that he had a grandmother who crossed the Line once on a trade run; no name, no line of descent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:319:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. Right ankle: ligaments, never seen by a healer, bound eleven days; no stick since day 64; runs on the gravel bar from day 65; "it bends less, and later". No burst at the ford or since. She killed one hound with the long knife. Her question stands unanswered in Cael's log. She has been told at Thornwater's gate that a healer would have had the ankle straight in an hour, and that there is none; she asked for nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:323:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. One point lit and put out at the ford; none since. Two pink lines across each palm; a pencil again on day 68. Holds: the hypothesis leaf; the finding (in Cael's log, by her dictation, and in the field archive in Lira's hand); a leaf headed *This side.*; the carter's map; and, in the middle box, the carter's wife's three sentences with *everybody knows* underlined twice. She has asked nobody what quiet ground is, Seln included.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:325:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze (not said in public). Lifted his Path once, under water, on day 53; killed the seventh hound. Unmarked. Walked the south road to the well first, alone, and said nothing. Has said aloud that he keeps waiting to be asked for his report. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut**; it spent the evening of day 53 in Thornwater's loft.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:327:**Objects and money.** Three boxes over the ferry drum. The reserve unopened. Board purse: **sixty-two marks earned** (18 + ford 40 + well 4); **fifty-two in hand** (one mark on flour and bacon on day 51; one to the hold for linen and thread; coppers unitemised). Hesk's satchel holds the log (with the finding and the seal entry), the old volume, the observation notebook, Pike's two lines on bark, and Hesk's letter. Cael's coat has lost its left sleeve. The ash stick is propping an old carter's shaft under the ash.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:329:**Pike's book and the wall.** **Six lines** under the five names: the protected ford line (said on day 60) and *The well at the south fork. Air cleared, shaft drawn, six stones set. Four marks.* (day 64). **Twelfth of thirteen; Teague eleven up.** The ford slip is with the finished slips, struck with one line through Teague's name and five strokes beneath, and Thornwater's mark at the foot. Fourteen slips on the plank on day 60; a bare tack set by the left-hand post on the evening of day 69 for a hold's slip expected from the north-west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:331:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. The hold's bowman saw one Wind burst and took it for a Path. The party now holds the stillhound finding in five sentences. **Quiet ground is three sentences from a carter's wife**; nobody has asked Pike or anyone. Thornwater knows the five as the crew that came up from its ford. The party knows from the hold that one healer walks a route and is not due, and that healers otherwise "stop inside, where the tiers are". Teague has read the struck slip and the line and said nothing; no meeting.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:333:**Open threads.** Two hounds gone down the river, logged as open. Why a hundred and ten yards; why dusk. What quiet ground is, and what a road bends round two days east of Thornwater. Lira's question. Hesk's letter and the roof. What Teague will say when they have cost him something. A hold's slip, with a ford in it, due on the oak in the morning.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:336:Movement 3 already carries the day-70 injury snapshot, fifty-two in hand, Teague out on two holds, the unmended ankle, and deployment count one (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:16-18,35-42`). Its author must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:339:- Seln used his native Shadow once under water; Cael's Shadow-adjacent fragment remains sealed and unused. Seln's case is shut and back on its strap, and his road reports remain unasked (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:17-25`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:407-415`; `manuscript/chapter-13.md:249-257`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:142`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:341:- Karis holds a new *This side* leaf, the carter's map bend two days east of Thornwater, and the wife's three-sentence quiet-ground rumor in the middle box with *everybody knows* underlined twice. Nobody has asked what it is (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:153-175,295-357`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-445`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:343:- Board/account state beyond the packet's purse figure: six earned lines, 62 earned total, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up; Pike has set a bare tack for the incoming unnamed ford slip (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-465`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:356:- **Oryn** is the first healer met past the Line. Tide as taught: contact only; about three serious mendings a day fed and slept, two on a road; cannot heal herself; "Because I cannot mend what I can't read."; the short reading (seconds) and the long one (both hands, all of her, minutes) — healing houses say surface and deep. The stall is named once. She knows NOTHING of fragments, has run no deep reading, records nothing and remembers. Her reading of Cael stopped at five; she said only "a river in the dark" and that it has no side she can find. "More than one" is NOT said (Movement 5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:358:- **Teague** learned nothing he could not read off a yard. Oryn told him only that she was late; he does not connect his lost day (waiting at a hold for the healer, for his bow's hip) to the five. Pike struck the ford off his hold; that cost him nothing because he chose the pass.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:360:- **Objects:** the hired cart and its load are lost (the ferryman's rope, blankets, kettle, canvas, flour); the smith's six is the only priced debt and the rope's replacement is open and unpriced. The three boxes are recovered; Brom's hedging bill and his older ash wedge survive. Cael's coat has lost both sleeves.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:365:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:366:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial (three bounded priorities), cold read (three clarity items), source-distance (6 tracked passages, no dense scene), plan / canon / protected-text audit (ten local line fixes — applied by the coordinator, one corrected: it is Pike, not Teague, who struck the ford off the hold). Sixteen of the author's 21 flags KEEP; five amended by line fix. Same-author repair r1 in progress when this block was written; the CLOSED note follows when the recheck returns.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:374:- **Brom's strap:** a doubled bight of the ferryman's long rope over his head and one shoulder, made fast low on the cart's near side; he draws with his chest and keeps both hands behind him. On the bench he walks on the up-slope side and leans against it. **The ferryman's rope went into the gorge with the cart.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:390:- **Teague (flag):** two holds' work in four weeks, a drain cut and a byre roofed; two mules. The bow's limp is an old hip that went out and seated itself wrong, ten years or more ago. Teague timed his second slip to meet the healer's round at the upper hold on the 81st and waited a day. On the hill above Oxhollow he asks her whether the hip is a thing she would do ("Not on a road. Not in a night."), and she tells him his five are in the yard ("They're not mine." / "No. They're not anybody's. I noticed that.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:393:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`) and the coordinator's ten audit fixes. Facts changed: Teague knows only that the healer was late, not why, and cannot set his lost day against the five; Brom's older ash wedge was not lost and lies with the three boxes; Oryn's sum now reads whole on the 99th, the long reading on the 100th at the earliest, four days of work at Thornwater's table beyond her stop and one day put on the route; Seln asks leave to go ahead and leaves scratched pebbles for word, and finds a clawless footmark at the first seep; Oryn washes her hands before she kneels, and checks her hands on Brom's wrist in the middle of the first reading; the ankle is asked for from the mule's back on the morning of the 82nd; chapter 18 has three scenes. Word counts, metrics, line numbers and flags elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures; the movement now stands at 41,346 words.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:395:**Calendar.** Dusk on the **eighty-fourth day past the Line**, on Oxhollow's bank. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term" twice; "frost"; "the next dry spell"). Days on the page: 70, 71, 72, 73, 74, 75, 76, 77, 78, 79, 80, 81, 82, 83 (in passing), 84; and, in Oryn's window only, 86, 89, 91 and 92. Teague's window is marked as the eighty-fourth day still. Weather: dry roads; first ice on a kettle on the 74th and frost on the bench each morning after; a cold rain on the 79th; milder in the valley. The next movement opens on Oxhollow's bank at dusk on the 84th, or the morning after.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:397:**Where everyone is.** The five are at Oxhollow, in the yard and at the ford, with three boxes on the ground against the gate-house wall. Oryn has gone north out of the gate at dusk with her mule, and is due at Thornwater on the 93rd. Teague and his three have crossed the ford southward at dusk with two mules, a day ahead of the five on the Lowmarch road.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:399:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst, day 53). Nothing was used on the mountain or since: Anchor, Compression, the Iron read, Wind and Storm all offered and were refused; Shadow sealed. **Three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped with five bands on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break, and Oryn means to lift the tape herself.** Left calf opened along the old bite on the 78th, bound in Oryn's linen, not mended. No log entries for the 78th and 79th. He has been read three times by a healer (the 80th, and twice on the 84th) and has answered three questions truly: his hurts knit in the right places; faster than other people's; no healer has ever got anything from him. He has not asked Oryn south. He has not answered Hesk's letter. Teague has spoken to him and he has said one word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:401:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. **One involuntary full burst on the 78th**, when the ledge went (her body travelled about twenty feet; the declaration and its crack crossed the gorge); a second refused, six yards short of shelter. **Right tibia broken on the 78th, set and mended on the 80th: straight, new, to walk within the week and not to be run on for a month.** **Right ankle never mended** ("That's a tape and a season. It'll set."); she asked once, from the mule's back, on the 82nd; she tapes it herself as Oryn taught her and says that she now knows where it is. Her right boot is under the mountain; she is barefoot on that side. She rode Oryn's mule from the shoulder to Oxhollow and has not said the word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:405:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **One declaration on the 78th: nine points and eight channels, no join longer than eight paces, held eight seconds. Empty since;** told to ask nothing of herself for a week from the 80th. She could not strike a flint on the 78th, wrote one line on the 82nd and held the purse on the 84th. Holds: the derived page (shale-backs), in her hand, with the ford finding beside it in Lira's; everything in the three boxes; the carter's map. Her word on the herd stays "derived": derived on the 75th and used on the 78th, and not tested, since the ledge went and the declaration followed in the same breath, which is two causes in an accident and not one cause in a test. She has met a primary source who keeps no book, and has asked her nothing she was not invited to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:407:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. No Path lifted. Unmarked. He asked leave on the 73rd to go ahead each day and find the sleeping place, and left scratched pebbles for word; he found every one, noted the pale rock, crossed the live slide for water, walked the lip twice and marked forty-four stones, and went down for help on the 80th, coming back alone ahead of the healer. He lent Karis his coat from the 78th. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.** He gave reports unasked on the 72nd, the 75th, the 79th and the 80th, since each bore.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:409:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, said by herself. She knows that she cannot read Cael, by surface reading, hurt or whole, and that his ribs knit "with nothing doing it"; she knows nothing of fragments and has no theory. She has promised him the long reading "when you're not broken". **Her sum (her window, the 92nd):** whole on the 99th by the rule, though her hands say sooner; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; her Thornwater stop ends on the 95th; she means to work four days more at Thornwater's table and has put one day on the route, for the reading. She is five days behind her round. She has mended six times on the page: Lira's leg and Brom's wrist (80th); a scald, a foot and a collarbone (84th); and, in her window, a shoulder at two mendings' cost (86th). She keeps no record. She told Teague on the hill only that she was late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:411:**Teague.** At Oxhollow's ford at dusk on the 84th he said his four things and crossed. He knows: no cart; a wrist in a healer's cuff; the girl's foot strapped; the small one asleep sitting up; the boy's ribs taped; that the mountain came down and all five came off it, mostly on their feet; that the keeper paid seventy for a no. **He knows that the healer was late to the upper hold on the 81st, where he had waited a day for the bow's hip, and he does not know why; he has not connected it with the five.** He does not know what Cael is. He and his three (the spear, the bow, the boy) and two mules are a day ahead on the road south.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:413:**Objects and money.** **The cart is in the gorge**, with the ferryman's rope, the blankets, the kettle, the canvas and the flour. Three boxes, whole, and Brom's ash wedge beside them; the reserve sealed in the third, unopened. Seln's case. Hesk's satchel, with the log, the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter and Pike's lines on bark. Karis's lantern, cord, brass straightedge and Hesk's clock. Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two marks earned** (62 + Oxhollow 70); **a hundred and sixteen in hand**; **six owed to the smith** for the cart. Pike's slip is in hand, with five strokes and Oxhollow's mark at its foot, to be carried to the plank. The long leaf was unrolled on the keeper's board and paid for there; the text does not say who carries it away, and the keeper is its buyer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:415:**Pike's book and the wall.** Unchanged since the 69th: six lines, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up. The traverse is not yet said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:419:**Open threads.** A fourth reading, promised at Thornwater in nine days and not possible, by her own sum, before the hundredth; and what four of the five felt when a healer said "both hands, and all of me". Twenty-one days of tape. Karis's reserve. A leg that may not run for a month and an ankle that will set. Six marks owed for a cart, and a rope. What Pike will write for a job that delivered a no and lost a cart. "The same contract inside a season." Animals lost from a hill, heard and not sworn, and twenty-five counted. Two hounds still open below Thornwater's ford. Lira's question, now with a job in it and a ledge under it. Hesk's letter, and no roof.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:422:Movement 4 already carries the dusk-of-84 location, 116 in hand / six owed, taped ribs, bound calf, new leg, missing right boot, Oryn north, Teague south, nine days to Thornwater, and the three boxes (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:18-20`). It must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:428:- Cael's three left-low ribs were broken day 78 and received five bands on day 81, to be lifted on day 99 by Oryn if possible; his reopened calf is only cloth-bound. His nine fragments are held, Shadow remains sealed, and deployment since the Line is one (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:121-155`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:3-45`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-333`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:429:- Oryn has failed three surface readings of Cael, knows only that he heals fast with no readable current, knows nothing of fragments, has run no deep reading, keeps no written record, and has put one day on her route for the promised whole-and-still reading (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:317-351`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:53-89,137-155,211-233`). Her mule still carries her panniers and covered crossbow; do not spend owner decision #24 early (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:143-159`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:103-107`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:430:- After fixes 6–9, Teague knows only what his own schedule and the yard/keeper show: he missed Oryn on day 81; on day 84 the five have no cart, have healer-made bindings, delivered a paid no, and all survived. He does not know they caused Oryn's lateness and knows nothing of fragments or the mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:237-295`; fixes 6–9).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:432:- The cart, ferryman's rope, blankets, kettle, canvas, and flour are in the gorge; the rope's replacement obligation has no price and must not silently alter the 116-in-hand / six-owed account (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:179-189`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:35-37`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-331`). The ash wedge survives with the boxes after fix 10. Cael's coat has no sleeves (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:17-23`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:433:- Pike's board has not yet heard the traverse: six lines, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up remain the last spoken standings until the marked slip reaches Lowmarch (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-465`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:174-176`). Hesk's letter is still unanswered, Lira's earlier question remains unanswered, and two stillhounds remain open downstream (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-451`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:329-331`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:435:**Movement 3 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the ten audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed (three more lines in Teague's window changed so he cannot tie the healer's lateness to the five); six tracked passages restaged; about 1,480 words of repeated survey procedure removed; orienting sentences at the split; the day-80 log reads "Some of the herd went over the edge after the cart. How many: heard, not sworn…"; a day-84 reset at Teague's window; Oryn's sum reconciled (whole on the 99th; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; a plan of four days at Thornwater's table plus one added day, which she changes at Thornwater's gate on the 93rd). New: Seln reads a heavy clawless footmark at a seep (unidentified sign; KEEP). Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES** — one applied (ch16: Seln shows the width with his hands). All six tracked passages RESOLVED, no new tracking. Gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected / 28 protected. 41439 words. Coordinator correction logged: the Bodies bullet first mis-stated whose leg was mended; corrected above and the Movement 4 author told.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:442:- **Cael's two private tests** (day 96, a quarter of an hour, a cord north of the stone, unwitnessed) are NOT deployments and are not logged as such. Deployment since the Line stays ONE. Shadow untouched. He has told nobody; his reasons are on the page and he distrusts them. The day-96 log omits the deployment line for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:443:- **Ring geometry — the manuscript governs (Movement 5 inherits):** the western line stone is 220 yards from the floor's middle; the floor is 26 of Cael's yard-strides across; the den is under the floor's EASTERN lip; so den to the western line is about 233 yards and den to the eastern perimeter about 207. The protected round is 1,374 yards and a piece (sixty-two cords and twenty strides); radius ten cords; the constant offset is six and a half feet per cord. NO cord length and NO stride length is stated, and none is to be added. "A hundred and fifty yards inside" is dropped from the plan.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:444:- **Sixty-two cords; stake 31; eleven uprights; eleven Ring sheets, all finished** on the 96th. The registry's stakes ring the place. No stillhound has been SEEN: prints and a den, all sign. The movement ends at dusk at the far lip, about to move.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:446:- **Pike spoke of Teague unasked, to the ledger:** Teague read the Fallow slip twice, put it back under the stone and took the fence. Teague has no stated reason. The two HOLD slips are unresolved ("a fortnight, then Teague").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:449:- **Objects and money:** Oxhollow's grain cart carried the boxes days 85–93; the ferryman's rope is owed in kind, unpriced; the purse ran 116 → 114 → 108; Seln's locked case is shut on his strap throughout (continuity beat added in repair). Letters: Ephram's says "Bracken" (he); Vell's carries "The session still stands," unexplained.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:452:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:459:- **Teague's crew on a road:** single file, a crew's length apart; no fire at any halt; chock-stones left as found; the mules at the windward end.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:460:- **The ferryman's rope (flag):** sixty yards of four-strand, laid up by himself. He will take no silver ("a figure's a thing you can pay and walk off from"); he will have a rope when they have one. Entered by Karis as owed, with no price.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:461:- **The two HOLD slips (flag):** one bark and one shingle; a bull to be brought down off top grazing before the snow, and a ford to be staked. Each hold "asked who". They will wait a fortnight for the five and then have Teague. Cael tells Pike on the 91st not to keep them past the fortnight. **They are still on the oak at the end of the movement.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:466:- **Eleven witnesses on the 91st:** Teague and his three; the Oxhollow carter; the hide-woman; the old carter under the ash; the shingle pair; the standing-money boy; the broker's clerk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:467:- **Teague (flag):** he has been round the Fallow Ring eleven times, with carts, by the ruts, at noon, and has never put it to the proof. He once saw a surveyor's kit, "years ago and a long way west". His reason for not taking the paper is his three; his sense that the paper is wrong has no reason, and he tells nobody.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:472:- **The long cord:** two box-ropes spliced by Brom, stretched from a fence-post, marked off with red wool against the short cord. **Its length is never stated**, nor is Karis's stride.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:474:- **The Ring's ground (flag; one picture for chapters 27–30):** at the crest of a long rise the ruts swing out to the north and come back to their line on the far side, keeping about forty yards from the line all the way round. The line crosses the old straight line of the road **eighty of Cael's strides** beyond the turn; Karis's grey stone marks it (the circle's western point). The camp is at the turn. The floor is three hundred yards from the turn. The perimeter is walked from the stone northward, with the ring on the right hand; Brom cuts a turf at each cord; the constant offset is **six feet and a half** to the cord.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:477:- **What each of the five reports inside** (beyond the protected lines): Karis can see where sixteen points would go and "can't find the hand to reach with"; this is not being empty ("reserve present, sigil gone"). Brom: "There's no next room"; a hundredweight weighs the same. Seln: "It is not there to be asked." Lira: a yard and a half, and no crack. Oryn: the surface count stops at "Four—"; returns at the stride; and stops when she alone is inside with Brom's wrist held across the line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:479:- **The floor (flag):** on the crown of a low swell, twenty-six of Cael's strides across by two diameters; colder than the turf; soundless under a boot; its rim rolled over like the rim of a dish, a hand above the turf outside and a finger above the floor within; level under a taut cord and under the brass and thread. Eleven squared grey uprights stand a stride in from the rim, each as thick as a man's body, the tallest twice Brom's height and the shortest knee-high. Round each, at chest height, and round the inner face of the lip, a band a hand wide of fine sunk lines, straight, hooked and crossing. None of Karis's forty-odd chips matches.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:485:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: the three markers are replaced by the protected units (ch25:43, ch25:131, ch29:169); Teague took a fence on the 89th (the upper inn's paddock, three days, five marks); Seln's locked case is on its strap on him at the ford, out of Thornwater's loft and over the line, shut; all eleven Ring sheets are finished (the tenth torn and done over); the bands run round the foot of each upright and no band on the lip is described; the den is found from above, at the box, and Seln speaks first; Cael's overrun is three quarters of an hour; Cael does not watch Lira's step. Word counts, metrics and line numbers elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:487:**Calendar.** Sunset on the **ninety-sixth day past the Line**, at the eastern lip of the Fallow Ring's floor. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term"; "frost"; "before the snow"; "fortnight"). Days on the page: 84 (dusk), 85, 86, 87, 88, 89, 90, 91, 92, 93, 94, 95, 96; and, in Teague's window, the evening of the 89th. Weather: frost every morning; dry roads; a north wind on the Fallow. The next movement opens where this one stops.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:489:**Where everyone is.** Six people at the den under the eastern lip, ten cords and half a floor inside the line: Cael, Lira, Brom (with the middle box on his back), Karis (with the eleventh sheet rolled in her coat), Seln (on one knee, the locked case on its strap across his chest) and Oryn. The lane trodden by the cord runs from the floor's western lip two hundred yards and more down to the grey stone. Oryn's mule is hobbled on the western side of the stone with her panniers, six of Thornwater's blankets, the carter's left boot and the long shape in its oiled cover still lashed on the pack. No hound has been seen. The sun is half under the hills.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:491:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** Logged deployment since the Line: one (the ford); the day-96 entry carries no deployment line. **On the 96th, unwitnessed:** the Iron read opened a pace short of the line and carried across it; a foot's worth of Wind evasion twenty strides inside; the Iron read once more on the floor. Shadow is sealed and untouched; it lifted at dusk on the 95th at the turn of the ruts and on the 96th inside the line, and was refused both times. Anchor asked at the stone and at the stake. Ribs: taped, eighteen days from the break, three to go. Calf: bound in Oryn's linen, closing by itself. He has told nobody that anything answered him inside, and has given Karis "It was dark before… It's dark now." for her sixth row. Hesk's satchel holds the log, the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter, Pike's lines on bark, and now Ephram's letter and Vell's. He has not answered any of the three.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:493:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst since the 78th; on the 96th she asked for a whole one inside the line and took one step of a yard and a half. Right tibia mended on the 80th: walking; not to run until about the 110th. **Right ankle not mended**, taped by herself; the carter's right boot over a torn shirt. Long knife drawn at the last line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:497:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Refilled: one point on a wick on the 93rd, "three parts full"; nothing since (roads). Inside she can see every place and set none. Holds: the perimeter table (sixty-two stations, one offset); the six-row table of the trials, with the sixth ruled on his statement; **eleven finished rubbings**, ten in the box and the eleventh rolled inside her coat; the carter's map with three pencilled rings, two marked *guess*; the registry's sheet; the long cord and the short one; the brass; forty-odd chips; the leaf with her nine crossings. She has said "A circle is a made shape." once, and nobody took it up.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:503:**Teague.** At Lowmarch on the 91st with his three. He read the Fallow posting twice on the 89th and put it back, and took a fence that evening (the upper inn's paddock, in sight of the ferry; three days, five marks); he has no reason against the posting and has given none. He watched the five take it. The two holds' slips are his if the five are not down inside the fortnight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:505:**Objects and money.** The middle box: chips, lamp, paper, ten rubbings (the eleventh is in Karis's coat), the two maps, the brass, the short cord. Seln's case on his strap. Two boxes in Thornwater's loft, the reserve sealed in the third, unopened. The Oxhollow cart has gone home with grain. Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and eight in hand.** Owed: one rope, sixty yards, four-strand, to the ferryman, with no price. A hundred marks lie in Pike's box against the broker's mark on the Fallow paper. Cael's coat has no sleeves.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:507:**Pike's book and the wall.** **Seven lines**; the seventh is the protected traverse line with *less six, the cart.* under it. **Tenth; Teague nine up.** The Fallow posting carries five strokes and is in Hesk's book. Two slips with HOLD and the five names are on the oak.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:509:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. All six know what quiet ground does to a live Arbiter, to the stride, and that a healer's hands stop there. The party knows that the registry's iron stands on the line, numbered thirty-one, some five years old; that no instruments are at the site; that hounds den under the floor. **Nobody but Cael knows that anything answers inside.** Pike, Teague, the clerk and the holds know only that five people took a paper.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:511:**Open threads.** Where eight or nine hounds are, at sunset. A lane two hundred yards long and one way out that anybody has walked. A healer who cannot mend east of a stone. A captain's three quarters of an hour. What he has not told them, and why. A posting written inside the Line for a thing that is not there. Thirty-one. Two blanks on a calfskin marked *guess*. "A circle is a made shape." A rope, two holds, three unanswered letters, and no roof.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:516:- **Correct Ring geometry:** western line stone to floor centre is 220 yards as printed; the floor is 26 of Cael's yard-strides across; the den is at the eastern lip. Therefore den to the western objective line is about 233 yards, and den to the eastern perimeter is about 207 yards. Do not reintroduce M4's discarded 150-yard figure (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:43-45,165-169,199-201`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:64-66`). The cord is approximately 21.9 yards by the protected circumference/radius figures, but its length and Karis's stride remain unstated (`manuscript/chapter-28.md:191-209`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:517:- **Lane:** the trodden cord-lane runs west from the floor through the western stone; the six are on the wrong/eastern side of the floor from it (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:9-29,199-201`). M5's 160-to-60 count must be staged within that longer approximately 233-yard retreat (`MOVEMENT-005.md:24`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:520:- **Secret/action count:** Cael alone knows the Iron read, foot of Wind and floor read worked. Shadow is unused; deployment since the Line remains one, and the day-96 log deliberately has no deployment line (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:239-299`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:63-77,219-235`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:526:- **Accounts/open obligations:** 108 marks in hand; one sixty-yard four-strand rope owed in kind; the two HOLD slips remain unresolved; the Fallow hundred remains lodged against the broker's mark (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:3-21,227-245`; `manuscript/chapter-25.md:229-253`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:181-185`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:527:- **Letters:** Ephram, Vell and Hesk remain unanswered in Hesk's satchel; Bracken is male and Vell's session remains unexplained (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:59-83`; `manuscript/chapter-27.md:55-101`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:169,189`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:531:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the seven audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Pike speaks unasked, to the open ledger); Seln's case carried on the page (Oxhollow's ford; the east gate; ch30's gear); four tracked passages restaged, the ch30 floor scene re-entered on the bands (Lira sees writing from the turf; the lip found when Brom's cord will not lie down; nine chips rejected and three families tried); ch28's survey proved once; two anchors; a cadence pass. Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES** — three applied by the coordinator: **Teague's fence is the axe-head hold's longer fence on the east road, forty marks, HOLD** (the repair's paddock job removed), and **Cael's overrun on the 96th is ONE quarter of an hour** (the repair's three quarters and the torn tenth sheet removed). Ruled KEEP: the cut bands run round the FOOT of each of the eleven uprights, a hand above the floor; no band on the lip; eleven finished, numbered sheets. All four tracked passages RESOLVED, no new tracking. Gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected / 36 protected. 37742 words. No markers remain.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:540:- **Inside the line** no companion Path was used: Oryn's hands had nothing ("Nothing in my hands"); cloth and knees. Nobody has theorized why the fragments answered. *Quieting* has still not been said. "Compact" has been said aloud once, by Seln. Nothing is known of where the file is, what it says or why; dating stops at "five years… maybe six". Seln's map memory (maps with holes) is open; he asked for the carter's map.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:545:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:560:- **What the reading is like from under it (flag):** it goes along the length of a person and returns to her other hand, at the pace she walks, favouring the right by a hair. He can tell where she is. As she passes: Wind turns over and settles; his palm warms; Compression does nothing; the read wishes to open; the ninth draws itself in small, unasked; the heaviest lies quiet. She says "You're helping." when his neck hardens.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:583:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **Nine points and eight joins for a count of six at the line on the 96th**; about a tenth left that night; nothing since. Throat mended on the 97th; hoarse single words by the 99th. Holds: eleven Ring sheets, dry, not yet looked at; the box unopened; the carter's map with three rings (two still *guess*) and Seln's charcoal sheet; her leaf *Where / Entered as said / Blank. Stamped. Filed.*; the stub and the entry against herself of the 99th. The two torn leaves lay on the loft's boards. She has asked him nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:589:**Objects and money.** Board purse unchanged: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and eight in hand.** The Fallow hundred lies in Pike's box; no instruments were found; the posting (five strokes) is in Hesk's book. The crossbow, with **five bolts**, is with the crew; its spanning hook is in the mule's near-side pannier. One bolt lies on the Ring's floor. Six blankets returned, one a hand narrow. The rope is still owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:593:**Pike's book and the wall.** Unchanged: seven lines; tenth; Teague nine up. The Fallow line has not been said. The two HOLD slips are unresolved on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:604:- **Counts/seal:** deployment since the Line is thirteen; Shadow has been used once and remains sealed; Oryn cannot identify Seln as its source and must hear sources by Path, not person (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:203-233`; fix 18; `MOVEMENT-006.md:26`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:607:- **Accounts/open threads:** start day 100 with 108 in hand; the Fallow hundred remains unpaid in Pike's box; one sixty-yard four-strand rope, two HOLD slips and three replies remain owed; the completion report travels west saying six; seven hounds remain untracked north/south along the outside (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:19,247-251`; `manuscript/chapter-33.md:193-195`; `manuscript/chapter-34.md:273-307`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:499-505`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:617:- **The debt:** three readings of himself, on three different days, then all of it to her at once, nobody on the road. OWED; the day is hers to set; NOT paid in this movement. The tenth has been used on nobody but himself.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:621:- **Named in this movement: *the Quieting*** (Karis, "because it is the right grammar": a process, not a place). **[UNBOUND] said once, aloud, as a limit.** Karis's hypothesis is NOT stated anywhere. The three standing words ("Still open. Still real. Patience.") are retired, with the reason. **"The still place" is not said in this movement**; it remains Cael's private log label from Books 5–6 and becomes a located, spoken finding in Movement 8.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:628:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:637:- **The Wind correction (flag):** he has always loaded a lean on the third count of Rooke's four-count; asked instead when the ground arrives ("four, and"), it costs half. Lira loads hers too.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:645:- **The ring laid flat (flag):** the eleven rubbings are long strips, each as long as a tall man and a hand and a half wide; laid like spokes on the barn's clay floor, each with a peeled wand for its stone's height (a thumb to a foot). Groups of strokes are copied on slips of bark; a grain of barley for each kind that recurs, in a horn cup; a bowl for the doubtful. **Her count is written, covered and not said.** She owns copies of nine alphabets, and the largest has fewer signs than she has grains.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:646:- **Why "the Quieting" (flag):** *quiet ground* is a carter's word for where; she wants the word for what happens; *the quiet* sits, *sleep* claims a will, *silencing* claims a voice; hers is made from a verb, takes a place after it, and claims only that it is one thing. **It is for the box:** asked whether it should go to Pike, she says that he and the carters have a word of their own and have kept alive by it, and that she will not hear hers in a meadow before she knows whether it is right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:653:- **The mule (C2, flag):** left with the crew on the 110th. She goes on the low side of nothing and the driver on the low side of her; she will not cross moving water with anybody on her near hand; her near hind has been shod since the Oxhollow road; she answers to a click; she has never had a name and is not to be given one. Oryn takes the off pannier on her own back and the spare rope, thirty feet of three-strand, for the next gate's jenny.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:656:- **The debt's terms:** three readings of himself on three different days; then all of it to her, at once and in order; nobody read on the road to find out whether he can. "If I'm at a table, you'll sit on the bench and wait your turn."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:672:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Unmarked. He has said that six sigils were on the road and five went out, and that he is counting it; that the west knows that something turns Paths off and does not know that something does not, "yet"; and that the record is kept. He said the birthday aloud. **Oryn has not been told that he is a source; she laid a hand on his shoulder on the 110th and said nothing. The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:674:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. **She knows the mechanism** (told on the 100th, with the nine by Path). Her hands are whole. She has set: on himself first; she is the one he tells; ask, every time; three readings on three days and then all of it; nobody read on the road to find out whether he can. She has not said what she would have answered, and has not forgiven him. She read Lira's arm on the 106th and the 110th. **She has left her mule with the crew** and gone north on foot with one pannier and a spare rope, **sixteen days late out of Thornwater and seventeen at Oxhollow**, to take the next gate's beast. She has said that she goes north at first light, that Oxhollow is seventeen days late, that Thornwater is on her route, and "Don't go in without me." She has heard no theory, since nobody has offered one.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:678:**Objects and money.** Three boxes; the reserve sealed in the third, unopened. **Oryn's mule, with the crew** (one empty pannier on the saddle). Hesk's satchel: the log (the rule, the note, the second pole, the birthday line), the old volume, the notebook, the letters, the broker's posting, Pike's lines on bark including the Fallow copy. The crossbow, hook and five bolts. Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and two in hand** (six to the hold on the 102nd). Owed: the ferryman's rope; the Fallow hundred lies in Pike's box unpaid. Hesk's parcel has not come; no boat has come in from the west since the 91st.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:693:- **Cael:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment thirteen; Shadow still only once; the eleven Wind leans are practice; the tenth has read only himself, once; two further self-readings on different days and the whole telling to Oryn remain owed; he may read nobody merely to test the ability; Oryn’s answer and remaining price stay withheld (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:245`; `chapter-40.md:189–211,319–385`; `chapter-44.md:167–209`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:695:- **Equipment and money:** 102 marks in hand; three boxes and Oryn’s mule; Seln’s shut case; Oryn’s empty pannier left on the saddle while she carries the other and the spare rope; the yard crossbow, belt hook and five bolts travel with Brom; the ring sheets, bark slips, four chips, calfskin rings and charcoal round remain in Karis’s boxes (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:55–67,379`; `chapter-41.md:3–39`; `chapter-42.md:205–277`; `chapter-43.md:171–215`; `chapter-44.md:209–245`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:697:- **Research state:** Karis’s kinds-count is covered and unsaid; finding four says only “five or six”; stake thirty-two remains Lira’s guess; the four wheres include two map rings marked *guess* and Seln’s unplaced childhood round (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:125–159`; `chapter-43.md:3–53`; `chapter-44.md:71–95`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:698:- **Open accounts:** Pike has eight completed lines but the crew has not heard the eighth read at the board; the Fallow hundred remains in Pike’s box, the ferryman’s rope and two HOLD slips remain unresolved, Hesk’s parcel has not arrived, three letters are unanswered, and seven hounds remain untracked (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:221–263,383`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:173–179`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:708:- **Shadow has now been used exactly TWICE and is closed for the rest of the book.** The seal was satisfied on the page: Cael a yard below the floor; Lira on the thirty-fourth step; Seln's back turned; the other three round the door's corner; the rim's six 260 yards off with no line below the hole's lip. Oryn does not know Seln is its source. What the rim has: a fence that failed at a knot set on the edge, and a boy who stood up and DECLARED outside. Teague saw the declaration from the ridge and asked nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:709:- **Tide and Oryn's condition.** At Millrace's bench on the 113th Cael asked leave to set his hand on a BOY'S wrist while Oryn held it, to learn what came to her hand, and was refused ("You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next."): the boy's leave was never his to ask from her, and the boy's treatment was not his lesson. On the road, an hour south of the fork, she opened it herself and he asked to read HER; she granted that, a different question, in her own words ("Yes. That's the answer, and I'm the one giving it… the same day as the lean-to and a different question, and… the rule held both times."). [Corrected at close from the Sol recheck: an earlier version of this bullet said she granted the same question.] "Self first" is honoured: he had read himself once (day 102) before reading her by leave. **The debt is still OWED:** two more self-readings on different days, then all of it to her at once; her day is hers; she refused a hurried second ("Not tonight"); nothing is forgiven.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:712:- **The Stair's chamber:** walls cut floor to roof in five courses, each as tall as a forearm; a line that is not on the Ring stands BETWEEN the courses, on its own, recurring "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride" — the Fallow's radius. (There is no continuous groove.) Karis paced the perimeter on the morning of the 115th and got two hundred. The open kit with its contents in taking-out order was found and is carried by Brom; **the case is untouched; the index and the stroke-and-bar are not decoded; nobody theorizes.** "Compact" is not said in this movement.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:713:- **Oryn** was at Millrace on the 113th (her circuit brought her round; EXC-B7-003), crossed for a wounded patient on the 114th and went down under a held rim on the 115th; she is a stop on her route — never "sixth", never "join". **Teague** forfeited a slip to come, held the rim unasked on the 115th ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"); his crew is unnamed; the healer of no Path has not appeared.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:714:- **#50:** Seln's "Six years I've wanted a face" stands verbatim and unglossed; the case's twelve years appears only in his window. **#51:** "Tomorrow makes three" is not explained. **"The still place"** is not said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:717:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:722:- **The chamber (flag; changed in repair r1):** ten strides square, as paced on the 115th; the roof is the underside of the floor above, without beam or crack, and stands **a hand above Brom's head** (Cael had called it a foot on the 114th, at a crouch; Brom's palm lies on it with the elbow bent). Dust as thin as the bloom on a plum. **The walls** are cut from floor to roof in five courses, each as tall as a forearm, in the same hand as the bands on the Fallow's stones (Karis can see the bars). **There is no groove.** What Karis keeps for the last of the oil is the protected finding: a line that is not on the Ring, on every wall, not in the courses but *between* them, on its own, recurring "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride, to the stride… at the perimeter's radius." How that spacing is read off walls ten strides long is not glossed on the page (repair flag 2). She samples the walls on twenty-nine sheets, and twice walks the foot of a wall with the short cord, counting.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:726:- **The second Anchor hand (flag):** the empty-handed one at the gate. The course is three lines, each as thick as a wrist, at the knee, the chest and over a tall man's head, thrown from forty paces across the old road from the old stake to the newer and on round the edge: "the same trade in a different hand… this hand threw", where the woman on the Ostrand road threaded nineteen fine points from fifteen feet. He keeps his hands inside his sleeves through the day. At the end Cael sees a pair of hands: a man's, broad, short in the finger, with a pale band where a ring was taken off before the work. Nothing else of him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:727:- **The knot (flag):** a single point as big as a fist, a hand above the turf, on the outer face of the **old** stake; three courses come into it from the south and three from the north (the two ends of one ring), and nothing comes out. Cael first looks for it on the newer stake, where the lines landed: "A rope is not made fast where it lands. It is made fast where the hauling starts." He lies in the north rut, reaches round the bar and lays his palm on it. How far round the edge the course ran is not seen; he feels "a great deal of it" run out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:728:- **The rim's bolts (flag): thirteen.** Gate bow eleven (Brom's shoulder; one during the run; eight ranging shots at the hole, the eighth down the stair to the thirty-first step; one at Cael outside the stone at dusk, which misses); north bow one and south bow one, lofted during the run; west bow none. They are too stout for the channel of the healer's bow (Brom tries one along the stock). On the 115th the boy lays the recovered shafts in a row by the four bows, Lira adds the one from the stair, and the head cut from Brom's bolt lies by the stone; the figure thirteen is given once, in the night log of the 114th. Teague reads eleven stirrup-prints "and a twelfth half made" on the brow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:732:- **The second paper's history (flag):** written at one desk and one sitting with the first (the same pricked margin, from a wheel with a tooth missing, so that every eleventh hole stands wide; the same fault in a letter's foot); sealed inside the same wrapper, with three hundred counted in a bag and a word of direction that it was not to be posted until the first was answered; kept in the broker's strong-box, he not knowing what it was; brought up by the clerk on the morning after the Fallow line was said; said twice to the meadow, and nobody scratched; read by Teague, who hung it on the nail himself, eight days before the 112th. It carries the hook and the bar.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:740:- **The fifteen:** a miller's man whose right hand went between the hoist's rope and its drum nine days before; a girl of three or four with a rattling chest, low and on the one side (not the child of the far gate); an old woman, small and upright, carried down the valley on a hurdle by two grandsons, who went through the fourth rung of a ladder getting a ham down ("It's got a ladder in it."); and a dozen with one hand each. Three mendings: "That's the day."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:745:- **Wind asked on the stillness:** he does not load on the third count; he asks on "four, and", when the bowman has gone entirely still (the gate-walk's "Shooting's stopping", by way of Lira).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:747:- **The 115th.** Teague's four on the rim: Teague on the brow, the spear south, the boy west, the bow north; Teague lends his horn lantern. The pacing runs from the stone northward with the Quieting on the right hand; Lira carries the cord's far end and finds the edge with her foot; Seln cuts the turfs; the old stakes stand within a boot of them; the round is the Fallow's, cord for cord, with the same odd strides.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:748:- **The kit (flag; order changed in repair r1):** found in the middle of the chamber floor. A cord knotted at every fifth span lies run out straight toward the eastern wall for half the room, with the rest of it in a coil that was never paid out ("measuring from the middle of that room to its wall, and had got half way"); then a mallet with an iron-bound head; a bar numbered thirty-two with the stroke and the bar, clean of rust; and a field ledger on its face, last and nearest. Behind them a flat case of board under tarred canvas, as long as a man's arm, with a shoulder strap, its lid thrown back and nothing in it. Karis: "a kit for one thing… He came to put iron on an edge." Seln: "They lie in the order that they came out… Nobody packs so. He meant to take them up again." One track in the dust came to it from the door; Seln cannot find it going out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:752:- **Teague (flag):** the slip is a shingle, nine days on the oak: *Millrace. Three stakes of the weir, gone in the last high water. To be set before the ground shuts. Four marks.* He has a day's posts still to set on the forty-mark fence. He tells his three the true reason at the fork and gives them leave to stay; none does. He sets two stakes and leaves the third, which forfeits the four marks. He once walked eleven cold terms beside a Wind, in another crew, and has worked beside two Embers. His unreported rank was earned on a ledge in the cold.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:756:**Calendar.** Late afternoon of the **hundred and fifteenth day past the Line**, at the stone on the eastern edge of the Long Stair, in full sun. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term", "frost", "the thaw", "the snow", "a dry month"). Days on the page: 111, 112, 113, 114, 115; in Seln's window, the night of the 112th; in Teague's, the 113th, 114th and the dawn of the 115th. Weather: hard frost every night, ringing roads, ice along Lowmarch's bank; no snow. The next movement opens where this one stops.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:758:**Where everyone is.** The six at the stone, with two mules (the brown, the crew's; the mill's grey jenny, Oryn's for now), three boxes, and the kit on the turf. Teague and his three have gone back up the ridge toward Millrace. The six from the rim went off north, south and west at dusk on the 114th and have not been seen since.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:760:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten confirmed fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: twenty-three**, by his own log (fourteen on the 113th; nine on the 114th; none on the 115th). **Shadow used twice in all** (the Ring; the Stair), unseen by anybody outside the circle who could carry it; it is shut again. Anchor: looked twice and unbound once. The tenth has now read one other person, with her leave, at one sitting; **he has still read himself once only**, and owes Oryn two more readings on different days and then all of it; she told him "not tonight" on the 113th. What he found in himself is unsaid and unnamed aloud. Body: the right forearm struck (bends on the 115th); a weal across the left palm, taped, unmended; hands warm again. He has said *Noted* twice to Teague. He holds the kit (Brom carries it). Hesk's satchel: the log, the old volume, the notebook, the letters, both of the broker's papers, Pike's lines on bark. Three letters still unanswered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:766:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. One point set, on her lamp, outside the stone on the night of the 114th. Holds: **forty sheets** (eleven of the Ring, twenty-nine of the Stair); **forty-one kinds, the same at both**, entered and underlined; **the line between the courses** (not on the Ring; on every wall of the chamber; recurring at ten cords and a piece, two hundred and twenty yards and a stride, the perimeter's radius), shown on the eastern wall's sheets; the Stair's perimeter table (the Fallow's round, to the stride); the surveyor's *Reach, edge to centre* figure, written down from Seln's reading; the leaf of the trials, inside her coat; the calfskin, with *guess* struck out beside the Stair's ring and still standing beside the far south-eastern one; the Ternhall brass, out of its cloth and held over the hide. Her hypothesis is unentered and unsaid. She has said that the floor was carved by somebody who knew the circle's size, and nobody took it up.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:770:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. **On the round's terms, as a stop:** "when I say lie still, you lie still, and when I say I can't help you, you believe me"; she goes when the round cannot spare her. Nineteen days late at the ford with the oxen by her own sum, "or more"; word sent north by a carter, with where to send for the child. Five mendings in two days (three at Millrace; Brom and Lira at the stone). She refused him at her own bench and offered on the road, the same day ("a different question"). She has been read by him once, short (one hand on her wrist) and long, and has been told what he found in her. She has not forgiven him, and has not been told what he found in himself. She does not know where the ninth came from. Her pannier and rope are on the grey jenny.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:772:**Teague.** He stood for the five at Lowmarch and sat at "eleventh". He hung the second paper on the nail. He took and forfeited a four-mark slip to be near; he saw one boy, outside the edge, declare a Wind, a fire and a third thing that he cannot name; he said only that he saw a man walk out of the Quiet declaring, and asked nothing. His three walked the ruts by lantern and brought in three crossbows. He held the rim through the 115th and lent a lantern. He still has a day's posts on the forty-mark fence. His crew is unnamed; the healer of no Path has not appeared.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:776:**Objects and money.** Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and two in hand**, unchanged. The three hundred lies in Pike's box against the broker's mark, and will not be marked. The Fallow hundred lies there too. **The kit:** case, pacing cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke and the bar and a bright turned point, mallet; the ledger apart, with Seln. Four crossbows by the stone, strings cut and locks empty, one broken; the rim's recovered shafts in a row beside them (thirteen loosed, by the log of the 114th), useless to the healer's bow. Karis's lamp filled; Teague's lantern returned. Owed still: the ferryman's rope; three replies; Hesk's parcel has not come.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:778:**Pike's book and the wall.** **Eight lines**; the eighth said twice in the crew's hearing on the 112th. **Eleventh; Teague ten up.** The Stair paper carries five strokes and **HOLD, on Pike's own mark**, said to the room and to be said to the meadow. Pike has said that his book has no column for what the eighth line means.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:780:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six. That the fragments answered at the Stair: the six. Which fragments, by Path: the six; where the ninth came from: the five. Teague and his three: a declaration outside the edge, of more than one kind. Pike and the room: that six went in at the Fallow and six came out. The registry's side: as above. Nobody has said why anything answers him inside. Nobody has put a verb between a made floor, an age with no ruler, the same round twice, a circle whose size the carvers knew, and a boy.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:782:**Open threads.** A bearing through two rings on a calfskin, and a third thing on it. A line between the courses of a wall that keeps a circle's radius, and that the Ring does not carry. A mark set twice, at two visits, that nobody will date. A surveyor who stopped in the middle of a line. An index and a two-stroke mark that Seln will not read. Six people who went off a rim without their bows. Two readings and a telling, owed. A healer nineteen late and counting, with a child whom she cannot hear. An arm that held a stair; an ankle that nobody has mended; a shoulder mended once. A captain who saw three things and asked nothing. A paper with HOLD on it that will never be paid. A fence at forty with a day's posts to set.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:785:Movement 8's packet already carries the day-115 rim, bearing, two mules, six people, Brom mended once, Lira closed again and Teague turning back (`MOVEMENT-008.md:18–20`). Its author must additionally inherit these surviving-prose facts:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:787:- **Cael and the debt:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment twenty-three; Shadow has now been used exactly twice and is closed for the rest of the book; Tide has read Oryn once by leave but Cael has still read himself only once. Two self-readings on different days and the full telling remain owed, Oryn's day remains hers, and neither her withheld answer nor forgiveness has been supplied (48:229–235,273–279; 51:197–225; 52:355–359).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:791:- **Knowledge limits:** the index, stroke-and-bar and last unfinished entry remain uninterpreted; Karis's hypothesis remains unspoken and unentered; nobody has theorized why Cael works inside; Oryn still does not know Seln supplied Shadow; Teague knows only that one practitioner walked out declaring (50:181–213; 51:239–257; 52:169–213).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:792:- **Open accounts:** the three hundred is taken and never to be paid; Pike's Fallow hundred, the ferryman's rope, Hesk's parcel and three replies remain outstanding; Teague forfeited the four-mark weir job and still has a day's fence posts (51:263–325; 52:355–359).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:794:- **Other people:** the six faceless attackers are gone with no attributable identity; Teague's three and every member of the rim remain unnamed; the healer of no Path has not appeared (51:91–103,263–383).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:796:**Movement 7 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the ten audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed; ch52's three tracked passages restaged (scene 2 re-entered on the bolt at the thirty-first step; the kit read from the cord inward); the design confirmed once; twice-told states removed from ch49–51 with the night log whole; the closing log's "five years ago" made to stand (the ledger's eight stations are the old irons, five cold terms by Seln; the stroke-and-bar is "two visits", the later undated; nothing decoded); a register pass. Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES** — seven applied by the coordinator: **what Cael asked at Millrace's bench is corrected to the source's actual distinction** (leave to touch a boy's wrist while Oryn held it — refused; on the road he asks to read HER — granted, "a different question"), with the bench's count and the day's log to match; and ch52 says Karis reads the radius figure from scaled divisions within the lone line, not as a spacing along the wall. All three tracked passages RESOLVED, no new tracking. Gates 0; overlap as below. 42413 words (the length ruled by the coordinator: the Stair's action not cut for the map's 40,000 line). Author-sourced sections above refreshed from the post-repair report; where they still describe the bench request as a request to read Oryn, the Tide ruling above governs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:798:**Movement 7, post-close correction (2026-10-11).** One of the recheck's own line fixes (ch47, "For the first time in his life, he…") produced an 8-word run shared with the source, which the overlap gate caught after the first publish. The coordinator recomposed the sentence ("He had never before asked leave to put his hand on another person. He had asked, and had been told that he might not…") and republished. Overlap now 0 unprotected.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:801:## AFTER MOVEMENT 8 — chapters 53–60, days 116–131 past the Line, THE BOOK'S LAST MOVEMENT (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method; repair r1 applied; CLOSED 2026-10-11 after Sol recheck r1)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:804:- **Deployment since the Line: TWENTY-SEVEN at book end.** Twenty-three after the Stair; then at the Hall on the 119th the read under water (24), Compression taken standing (25), an Anchor point laid by hand in the breach and held (26); and on the 120th Tide on Oryn, asked and granted, one sitting (27). The Anchor point set as a trial on the 118th is NOT counted ("I'll not call a trial a use"), which agrees with the protected inventory: Anchor used twice this year, once each way (the Stair's unbinding; the Hall's holding). Self-readings are not counted. **Shadow was not used**; it has been used exactly twice in the book and remains sealed; Oryn does not know Seln is its source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:805:- **The debt is paid.** Three self-readings on three different days (the 102nd; the night of the 119th; before light on the 120th), then all of it told to Oryn at once, and she was read only with her leave. **"The still place"** — Cael's private log label since Books 5–6 — is now a LOCATED finding in him and has been said aloud: to Oryn first, and to the other four on the 121st. Shape and sensation only: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log." No theory, no source, nothing about before.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:806:- **Teague is neither read nor asked** and knows nothing of the mechanism. He forfeited the four-mark weir slip to come (it was never set or paid); the axe-head hold's fence (forty) passes to the five for the cold term ("Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road," / "Ours,"); "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew is unnamed, the older healer of no Path included.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:807:- **The fourth site:** not entered, not named, its effect on a Path UNKNOWN and untested. Lira stopped one pace above the iron; the cordon's bars mark the line; nobody crossed and no sigil was tried. No watch-post; no dating on the cordon; the silhouette is ambiguous. Four stakes have been seen in all, each alone at an edge.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:809:- **Sheets: fifty-two** (eleven Ring, twenty-nine Stair, twelve Hall). The survey kit is on the table at Lowmarch: the case in tarred canvas, a cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke and the bar and a bright turned point, never driven, and a mallet; the dead man's ledger, shut, is Karis's (Seln gave it to her). The case of Seln's is shut and untouched; nothing is decoded.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:810:- **The end, at Lowmarch:** first snow on the 129th; the last ferry on the 130th with two letters west (Hesk; Vell) and Ephram's deferred to the first boat of the thaw; ninety-six in hand; nine lines in Pike's book and no number against the season; eleventh on the cloth; the ferryman's rope still owed. The instruments read true in Cael's hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:815:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:816:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial, cold read, source-distance (**0 tracked passages**), plan / canon / protected-text audit (nineteen line fixes applied by the coordinator: the protected units restored, the final count corrected to twenty-seven, Teague's forfeited slip, the fourth site kept strictly outside, three extra maker or intent assertions removed, the kit itemised).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:819:- **The brass on the hide (flag).** The Ternhall strip is slid down along itself with a pencil dot (a ruler "as long as its owner is patient"). Laid through the Fallow's ring and the Stair's, it runs into the carter's water-strokes and passes his third blank **a finger outside** Karis's pencilled ring. She moves nothing on the 115th. On the 120th she rubs the ring out and draws it where the cord put it, with *moved; paced.* On the 123rd she adds a fourth ring "at the very edge of the skin", with no word beside it; by the 131st a fine pencil line is ruled through the three centres and the fourth ring and off the hide. **What a ruler on a map of days is worth:** "a direction that is good to the breadth of this pencil at the length of my arm… a strip of country a mile wide." On the ridge she carries the line by ranging: Seln a furlong ahead, the last resting-place behind, moved until the three lie in a row. No compass direction is claimed for the line as a whole (ruled KEEP).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:822:- **The Drowned Hall's ground (flag; one picture for chapters 53–56):** a basin "as round as a plate"; reeds and black water to the line and no farther (the same perimeter as the other two, sixty-two stations, by cord on the 120th); a causeway of the old grey, a stride wide and a hand above the water, **a hundred and eighty-five yards** from the grey stone to the kerb; **the kerb, "the hall's outer coping"**, two strides broad round a dish seventy yards across, holding a foot or two of clear moving water over a floor broken into great plates with round edges; in the middle the hall, twelve strides square, walls a yard through, three times Brom's height at one corner and chest-high in two places, with lengths of an old coping still standing on the wall-tops, cut on the inner face in courses ("nine deep where the wall was whole"); one gap with a sill of the grey; inside, a ledge three or four strides broad round a breach "as wide as a cart is long", where the spring stands up in a low dome; one great slab aslant in the breach (it slides down into the depth when the point is let go).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:823:- **Stake thirty-three (flag):** one, at the track's end, a boot's width from Karis's stone; scaled in leaves like the old ones; the registry's stamp and two figures, "and nothing beneath them". Seln: five cold terms, "of an age with the Fallow's, and with the old one at our last stone… the same mallet drove all three"; no second. **A second stake on the kerb**, a few yards from the causeway's head, bent over at the height of a knee "like a nail that's been struck from underneath"; not examined closely and not numbered on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:826:- **Anchor, as first set (flag):** by contact only, his palm on the surface; it "went down his arm as a plumb line goes down a well, and there was a point under his hand"; it stays when the hand is taken away, for as long as he holds it; he can see it at arm's length and feel it "as he would have felt his own finger kept upon a line of a page". A held plate cannot be tipped. Held against a biting thing, it takes everything else that he has. No range beyond contact, no rate and no limit of time is assigned. **The first point he ever sets is the trial of the 118th, which his log does not count as a deployment.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:833:- **Karis's leaf of the three places (flag):** one leaf made four times: one for each box and the first in her coat with the trials leaf. On it: the three names; perimeter and radius; the stake numbers; the sheets (eleven, twenty-nine, twelve: fifty-two); *one wall; thirty-three of the forty-one; none strange; a sample, and no more*; *The lone line is present. Divisions seen; not counted; not measured.*; the surveyor's *Reach, edge to centre* figure, copied from the book held open by Seln; *The three middles lie on one straight edge, as near as this skin can show.* One line of the leaf is left clean. She tried to make the brass miss and could not; she had laid the ruler herself, before the third place was known.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:834:- **Teague's healer (flag; unnamed):** "sixty, or near it, as lean as a rake", grey hair knotted under a cap, a much-mended satchel, a staff that she does not lean on; no Path that mends ("I've no Path that knits"); forty cold terms of binding; with the crew for nine, since "a ford with a carter's leg in it"; she spends the dry months at her daughter's hold up the north water and comes down at the first hard frost. She carries a splinting board, four yards of webbing and raw wool. **The binding:** a pad under the arm; webbing round the chest, over the point of the shoulder and back beneath the elbow, three times, with "a drover's" turn (under, and back on itself) that keeps the weight on the ribs and off the joint. Oryn asks to be shown it twice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:835:- **Teague, days 115–121 (flag):** **he did not set the weir's third stake; the ford-keeper did not mark the shingle; the four marks were lost, as Movement 7 closed it.** He sent word to Pike by the mill's carter ("five strokes to look at, and all of them walking; and the three hundred was to stay where it lay"); followed the trail from the Stair for three days "for what's behind them, if there's anything", walking back a mile along it at each dusk; found nobody on it. He hears Karis's sentence and Cael's ruling on the 121st, watches the brass run off the hide, and asks nothing. His five reach Lowmarch before the five do.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:838:- **The fourth site, as seen (flag): OUTSIDE ONLY.** From the crest at dusk on the 123rd: "a great shallow head of pale ground, scooped out of the hills… and open toward the south"; no bird or beast; in the middle a thing "grey, and upright… taller than a man", with "a top that was not level" (Lira: "It's not one thing, I think. Or it is, and there's sky in it. I'd be guessing."). Two faint old ruts, with turf in them, go round the valley's head high up. **The cordon** lies about a hundred and ninety paces below those ruts: bars of the registry's pattern, one to a pace, each stamped *thirty-four* with the stroke and the bar beneath; Lira counts forty to the left and Brom forty to the right, and it goes on. **Lira stops one pace above the iron, at about a hundred and eighty-nine paces; her sigil is not tried; nobody says "Gone" or "Back"; nobody touches a stake; nobody crosses.** Cael "knew only that he had crossed three such lines before and that the fragments had answered there; nobody had tested this line, and nobody would." Seln puts no date on the cordon and nobody assigns a purpose to whoever set it. Karis lays the long cord twenty times along the feet of the bars, from outside: the short measure comes to half of what it has always come to. Her notebook's sum: **four hundred and forty yards, and two strides**. What the line does to a Path is unknown; Lira's question stands unanswered. Seln: "There was a sheet with two… A marsh three days behind us, and this: I can place it now."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:840:- **The inn (flag):** the lower inn's keeper is "a slow heavy man with a cloth over his shoulder". The back room is "the store behind the chimney": narrow, one small window, a deal table, meal-sacks, warm from the back of the hearth. Six marks for the cold term; the five may lie at the hearth's end "for the standing-money… as long as there's paper in my store". A small window at the far end of the hearth looks down on the landing. **On the table:** the kit's case in tarred canvas, with the strap coiled on the lid; inside it a cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke and the bar and a bright turned point (never driven), and a mallet; beside it the dead man's ledger, shut; the three boxes against the warm wall; fifty-two sheets in three heaps.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:842:- **The last ferry (flag):** on the 130th, at noon, through a lane cut in the shelf ice; the post comes down to the far bank with the courier of day 4 (the hat with one side cut away). **Nine pieces:** the smith; the upper inn (a bill); two for the landing broker under his own seal; the hide-woman; a hold at the top of the north water; Teague's healer, from her daughter; Thornwater; and Hesk's parcel ("From a town I never heard of"). Hesk's straightedge is "a hand longer than the one from Ternhall, and a little broader". Cael's two letters go back by the same boat, with the clerk's packet. The ferryman and his boy take the hauling rope off the drum and coil it in the shed; the gelding goes to the smith's stable. The rope is still owed: "I'll not want it this side of the thaw."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:844:- **Roles (all unnamed):** Teague's healer; the hide carter (a scarf over his nose); the inn's keeper; the ferryman and his boy; the courier; the old woman and one grandson; the stooped carter; the Thornwater carter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:846:### BOOK END STATE — for Book 8 (author, as updated after repair; the rulings above govern)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:847:**Calendar.** The morning of the **hundred and thirty-first day past the Line**, at the hearth of the lower inn at Lowmarch, with a hand's depth of snow on the sill. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term", "frost", "the thaw", "first snow", "a ring round the moon"). Days on the page: 115 (dusk), 116, 117, 118, 119, 120, 121, 122, 123, 124–128, 129, 130, 131; in the windows, 117–120 (Teague), 119–120 (Karis), 124 and 127 (Seln), 122–128 (Oryn). Weather: a mild spell on the 116th–118th; hard frost from the 120th; a ring round the moon on the 126th; a north wind from the 127th; the first flakes at Lowmarch on the afternoon of the 129th; two fingers of snow on the 130th and a hand on the 131st. Shelf ice a cart's length broad on each bank. **The ferry made its last run on the 130th and its hauling rope is taken in.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:849:**Where everyone is.** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln at the lower inn, sleeping at the hearth's end, with the store behind the chimney for the paper. Oryn at Thornwater, two days up a saddle that the carter does not expect to cross again before the thaw; she meant to go north by the wicket when the bench was paid, and her letter was written on the evening of the 128th. Teague, the spear, the bow, the boy and the older healer at Lowmarch for the cold term.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:851:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten confirmed fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: twenty-seven** (the ford 1; the Ring 12; Oryn on the ridge 1; the Stair 9; the Hall 3; Oryn at the marsh 1). The trial point at the Hall's kerb on the 118th is logged and not counted. Shadow used twice in all and shut. Anchor: looked three times; unbound once (the Stair); a point set twice, of which one is the uncounted trial and one held the breach. Tide: Oryn twice, each time by her leave; himself three times (102, 119, 120); nobody else; never inside a line. **The still place:** his old log label, now a location under the breastbone, read three times; nothing moves in it; all ten go round it and none through; they do not pile against it; not the Quiet; not a fragment; told to Oryn at once and in order on the 120th, and to the other four in three sentences on the 121st; he has been told to write it down and stop touching it, and has not touched it since. Body: ribs quiet since the morning of the 129th; right forearm and left palm no longer remarked; calf a closed seam. Hesk's satchel: the log (the entries of the 118th, 119th, 120th, the fork, the crest, and the inventory of the 129th), the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter and note, Ephram's and Vell's letters, both of the broker's papers, Pike's lines on bark, and Oryn's letter on bark. **He has Hesk's brass straightedge, and it reads true in his hand.** He has said "Noted" to Teague three times. He has not answered Ephram.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:853:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst in this movement. **Left arm slung high, all eight marks taken (read by Oryn at the fork on the 122nd), still under the order: it holds nothing until Oryn says, and she has not said; five weeks on the 131st.** It took no part in her two shots in the Hall, and it held nothing in a fall on the ice on the 127th. **Right ankle taped, never mended**; she walks on the whole sole; Oryn left her a roll at the fork. **She carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap, spanned, with one bolt in it**; she cannot span it; she shot it twice in the Hall, one-handed, and hit twice. She has not asked for the ankle again. She has not crossed, touched or tried the fourth line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:855:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. **Right shoulder: bolted on the 114th and mended; opened on the Hall's wall on the 119th and mended a second time ("It will not hold three times this season"); bound on the 120th by Teague's healer and Oryn in four yards of webbing, with a drover's turn; the knot not to be undone except by that woman, who looked at it on the 129th and said "It'll do."** He carries the kit on his left side. He lays six bowls and, since the letter, has left the sixth out. He took the fence: "Ours,".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:857:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Points set on a fire and a lamp only, always outside a line. **Fifty-two sheets** (eleven, twenty-nine, twelve), in three heaps in the back room. **Forty-one kinds** at the two sites done properly; thirty-three of them, and none strange, on the Hall's one wall; the lone line seen there and not measured. Three perimeters of one size and the fourth site's radius by the bend, from outside: four hundred and forty yards and two strides. **The kit's field ledger, given her by Seln.** The leaf of the three places, in four copies (one to a box, one in her coat with the trials leaf). **The carter's map with four rings, the third moved and the fourth unlabelled, and a pencil line through the three paced centres and on off the hide.** The Ternhall brass. She has said "Someone made this pattern." once, aloud, and nobody answered. **Her hypothesis is unentered and unsaid.** She paid six marks without counting and keeps the purse.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:859:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Unmarked. He shot twice in the Hall and hit twice. He wrote in Karis's book with his own hand. He gave away the ledger. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.** He has placed "the sheet with two" (the Hall and the fourth site). He has not named the index, the stroke and the bar, or a date for the cordon. Oryn does not know that he is the source of Shadow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:861:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. At Thornwater, "on the route". **She has been paid what she set**: three readings, and all of it told, with his hand on her wrist; she has said "It's paid." **She has not forgiven him, and the answer that she kept is still kept.** Her finding stands: she has never felt such a thing in anyone, and does not know what right would look like in him. She has no theory and has been offered none. She knows the mechanism, and the nine by Path. She has the mill's grey jenny, her pannier and rope. Her own brown mule is with the crew. She was three weeks late at the ford with the oxen on the 125th. The old woman's knee, mended at Millrace on the 113th, has held. Her letter: *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:863:**Teague.** Unread and unasked. **Four marks poorer for the weir slip, which he forfeited.** He knows: six went into the Fallow and came out; one walked out of the Stair declaring more than one thing; six came out of the drowned hall wet; a strip of brass runs through three places on a hide and off its edge. He has asked "What are you." once and been answered "I don't have one." He knows nothing of the mechanism or of anything working inside a line. His term: "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." He has given the five the forty-mark fence and has the cold road. His crew is unnamed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:865:**Pike's book and the wall.** **Nine lines** under the five names; the ninth is the Stair, with *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The season line said and written. **No number against it.** **Eleventh on the cloth, unchanged.** He has turned the ledger toward Cael once. The Fallow hundred and the Stair's three hundred lie in his box unmarked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:867:**Objects and money.** **Ninety-six marks in hand** (a hundred and two, less six to the inn). The reserve sealed in the third box, unopened. Three boxes against the warm wall of the back room. **The kit on the table**: the case in tarred canvas, the cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke and the bar and a bright turned point, the mallet; the ledger beside it. Two brass straightedges. The brown mule (the text does not say where she is stabled). Oryn's crossbow, hook and one bolt; four bolts are in the wold-wyrm. Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman, "not this side of the thaw"; a reply to Ephram. The fence at forty is taken and not yet begun.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:869:**The Quieting, as known.** Four sites on one edge of brass. The Fallow Ring (stake 31), the Long Stair (32, on two bars, one with the stroke and the bar; the same mark on the kit's unused stake) and the Drowned Hall (33, old, no second) entered. The fourth seen and paced from outside on the 123rd: twice the radius by the bend of its cordon; stakes numbered 34 with the stroke and the bar, a pace apart; old ruts kept a hundred and ninety paces off; a standing grey shape that nobody could make out. **Not entered, not named, not dated, and not tried: no Arbiter has been taken to that line and what it does is unknown.** At the other three the live Arbiters stop at the line and Cael's fragments answer inside; whether a line twice the size does anything more is Lira's question and is unanswered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:871:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six. The still place: the six. That fragments answer inside a line: the six. The Compact's side: a completion report on the Fallow; what the rim saw at the Stair; and now a clerk's packet saying that a crew kept a kit. Nobody outside the six knows that anything works inside. Nobody has said why. Nobody has put a verb between a made circle, an age with no ruler, four on a line, and a boy.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:873:**Words said aloud.** *The Quieting* (Karis's, for the box; once more at the Hall's stone). [UNBOUND] once, in Movement 6, and not since. "Compact" aloud once, by Seln, in Movement 5; in this movement only in Cael's log and his letter to Vell. "The still place" aloud to Oryn and, by its description, to the four. "Someone made this pattern." once. "wold-wyrm" and "the drowned hall" as a carter's words, by Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:875:**Open threads.** A line that runs off the edge of a calfskin. A fourth circle behind a fence of iron, and a thing in it that the dusk kept. Whether twice the size is twice anything else. An arm to be released by a healer two days off, and an ankle that nobody has mended. A shoulder in webbing that will not bear a third mending. A captain's term. A fence at forty. A number that a book-keeper would not write. A dead man's ledger with an index and a mark that nobody will read. A locked case. A place under a breastbone, left alone. A rope. A letter to a friend on a bluff. And a question that was asked once at a table, which nobody answered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:883:- **Opening instant and place:** morning of day 131 at Lowmarch's lower-inn hearth; first snow began day 129, last ferry ran day 130, hauling ropes are in, and a hand's depth lies on day 131 (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:127-145`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:31,47-95,221-225`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:884:- **Party locations:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, and Seln are at the lower inn, with the warm store behind the chimney for the archive; Oryn is at Thornwater and her letter asks them after the thaw to bring the map; Teague's unnamed four practitioners plus the unnamed older healer are at Lowmarch for the cold term (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:221-247`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:3-25,131-217,221-237`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:885:- **Cael:** nineteen; ten fragments; final deployment **twenty-seven after fixes**; Shadow used exactly twice and sealed; Anchor used twice, once each way; Tide has read Oryn twice in all, each by leave; Cael has read himself three times and has not touched the still place since Oryn's order (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:169-301`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:29-41`). His Hall rib bill goes quiet on day 129 (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:49-51`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:886:- **Still place/debt:** old private label, now a located and spoken finding; under the breastbone; nothing moves; all ten go round and none through; no piling; not the Quiet; not a fragment; older than the log; Oryn heard all of it at once while granting the reading of her body, declared the three-and-telling debt paid, withheld forgiveness and her old answer, and ordered it written and left alone (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:169-297`; `manuscript/chapter-57.md:191-209`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:39`). All six know the finding; only the six know the mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-57.md:191-209`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:889:- **Karis/research:** Ember, Iron Rank Three; voice whole; 52 sheets split 11/29/12; forty-one kinds at the Ring/Stair and thirty-three seen on the sampled Hall wall; four copies of the three-site leaf; carter's map with four unlabeled/aligned circles; Ternhall straightedge; kit field ledger; hypothesis unspoken and unentered (`manuscript/chapter-57.md:3-87`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:17-27,239-255`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:892:- **Board/work:** five names remain eleventh; nine completed lines; no number on the first-snow season line; Stair price says “three hundred; taken; not paid”; Teague's exact term is “After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.”; the five take the forty-mark fence, whose day's posts and far side remain to do (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:167-247`). Teague's four-mark weir slip remains forfeited after fix 8.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:893:- **Money/accounts:** ninety-six living-purse marks (102 less six); sealed cart-and-gelding reserve still unopened in the third box; Fallow hundred and Stair three hundred remain in Pike's box and are not crew-payable debts; ferryman is owed sixty yards of four-strand rope, not wanted before thaw; fence not begun (`manuscript/chapter-52.md:357`; `manuscript/chapter-59.md:145-157,175-179,241-247`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:7-11,31`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:894:- **Objects:** three boxes; kit case/cord/stake 32/mallet on the back-room table after fix 18; kit ledger beside it; 52 sheets; map; Ternhall and Hesk brass straightedges; Hesk's satchel/log/old volume/notebook; Seln's shut case; brown mule with the five; grey jenny with Oryn; Oryn's bow/hook/one bolt with Lira; four spent bolts in the Hall (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:269-317`; `manuscript/chapter-58.md:23-27,59`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:15-25,59-75`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:895:- **Letters:** Hesk's parcel/straightedge arrived; Cael sent Hesk and Vell replies west, including Vell's “session still stands”; Ephram remains unanswered but is promised the first thaw boat; Oryn's exact bark letter is carried in Hesk's satchel and needs no answer (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:59-89,213-227`). The clerk's packet says only that the crew kept the kit (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:87-89`). OWNER #25's Lira-family line remains opaque and receives no new setup.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:896:- **Knowledge limits/open pressure:** Teague/Pike/holds/Compact do not know the mechanism or that fragments work inside; Oryn knows sources by Path but not Seln as Shadow source; no theory connects the sites, still place, or Cael; the cordon has no watch-post or date; the central shape has no name; the line runs off the map; the unanswered questions are twice-size effect, who/why, the unopened case, the archive index/mark, Ephram's reply, the rope, and Oryn's withheld answer (`manuscript/chapter-56.md:155-197`; `manuscript/chapter-58.md:117-229`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:85-89,239-267`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:903:- **A4 changed to final state:** Cael's debt is paid in the correct direction; Oryn is at Thornwater; ask-first stands; she still does not know Seln is Shadow's source (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:231-297`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:131-217`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:906:- **A7/B9 changed to the final seam:** deployment twenty-seven after fixes; Shadow exactly twice and sealed; the M7 rules remain, with new bills only for contact-set Anchor, Compression ribs, and the permitted Tide reading (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:179-293`; `manuscript/chapter-55.md:155-163,235-301`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:907:- **A8/B11 changed from forecast to confirmed resources:** use the complete money/object/debt state above; withdraw only the old forecast `nothing owed`, because the ferryman's rope and Ephram reply remain open (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:145-157`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:85`).
