books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-4-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-5-Dry ground, rising. The Span's far rim was behind them by half a day, and the land east of it went up in long steps of grass and shale toward a line of hills that had a notch in it, low and square, where the bearing went; and Seln had looked at the notch from the last step at noon, for a long time, with his hands in his coat, and had said "Pass," and nothing else, and had not looked at it again, which from Seln was a paragraph. Beyond the hills, by the office's distance from a hold, the point. A day, or two. Karis had said she would pace it and she had not paced it yet, because the pass was between her and it, and she did not pace a thing she had not stood on.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-6-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md:7:Twelve, and a mule, and a fire on the shale with the wind off the hills taking the smoke away east ahead of them, as if the smoke had somewhere to be. The broad man on a stick — Vastin's second one, cut on the crest and given without comment, so that there were two men on sticks at the fire and neither of them mentioned it. Teague's arm in Oryn's wrapping, elbow to wrist, and the hand at the end of it doing nothing, because she had told it to. Karis's hand bound and the notebook in it. Vastin, the twenty-sixth day of a month. Brom with two bruises that he had not shown anyone and that Oryn had read through the coat and left alone, because a bruise was a bruise. Oryn, two days past the end of the road that had been hers and one day into the road that was not, walking as she walked, on her terms, which she had not restated, because she had said them at a ford and once at a ford was a term.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-8-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-9-And the blanket.
