books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-108-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-109-The older woman with the cloth bag bound it after. Oryn let her. That was the third thing between the two healers, and it was not a look and not a nod; it was one of them putting her hands in the other's work, at the other's leave, and Cael entered it as the largest thing yet, and the least said.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-110-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md:111:Teague's arm she read and did not touch. "Tomorrow's a pass," she said. "I know what a pass does to a man who leads from the front of it. Lead from the front of it with the other hand." Teague said "Noted," which was the third time from him too, and Oryn said, "I'm going to have to find another word," and did not, and went to the mule.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-112-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-113-The watch had gone east. That was the last thing on the shale before the fire went down, and it was Seln's, and he said it as he said things, to the hills, from the camp's edge, with the cache beside him.
