books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-19.md-126-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-19.md-127-That was the price, and she did not hide it. "Nobody died of that," she said, when she could stand, to the older woman, who had not asked, and the older woman nodded, once, which she had not done at the ford, and that was the second exchange between the two healers, and it was a nod.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-19.md-128-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-19.md:129:Teague's arm was the other price. He had it under his coat by the time Oryn came up the slope, and she said, "Arm," and he said, "Contract," and she said, "I don't read contracts. Arm," and read it — the wrist, the elbow, the shoulder, along the line — and said, "You've done that twice in a fortnight. A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint. That's not a healer's opinion. That's a fact about a line." Teague said, "Noted," and she said, "Everybody says that now," and wrapped the elbow properly.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-19.md-130-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-19.md-131----
