editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-359-11. **Cleon's goodbye (S17):** "Work. Not a finding." / "Mind the stair. It leans."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-360-12. **Fragment eleven (S12):** "Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. A plane, not a body: the ground told not to give. Distinct from the third — Iron-adjacent, the bed; this is not the bed hardened, this is a line drawn on it and kept. Engagement field: defensive; rooted. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-361-13. **Fragment twelve (S13):** "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth." Then: *He looked away. Kept.* *Not a man.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:362:14. **Fragment thirteen (S19):** "Force-adjacent. Teague. Partial. Bronze. Impulse along the line of the frame at contact: from the ground, through the man, out at the hand, and nothing to either side of the line. Needs a thing to push against — the barricade, the ground under the feet; nothing at a distance; nothing from the air. A body's length. The cost back along the same line, every time, at the place the line comes out. Engagement field: close; braced. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Thirteenth."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-363-(Notice typography follows the edition's convention for system text. The notices must read aloud as prose.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-364-15. **Hesk's dividers note (S14):** "A rule says a line is true. A divider says how far, and carries it. You've the first. Here's the second, and mind the points; they'll go through a thumb as easy as a sheet. Lines are for finding out how far a thing is from another thing. Everything is. — H."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:365:16. **The grade (S17):** "A mark is a grade. The one they give a boy at fourteen says what he's *for*." … "The one on a sheet says how *old* the thing is." / "Somebody laid them down in order" / "It's observation. I'm telling you what the paper says. Not what it means." / Teague: "Oldest last." … "Then that's where we're going."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-366-17. **Pole two (S16):** Lira: "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Cael: "Since my Kindling I thought the system forgot to make room for me," … "It didn't forget. It was *built* so there'd be no room. Four hundred years of a whole world, so that I wouldn't happen." … "I happened anyway." / Lira: "Yeah." … "Now what." / Cael: "Now we find out how old the oldest one is. Karis has a bearing and the marks, and the records to read them against. There's a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine." … "I want to stand in the middle of it." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-367-18. **Vastin at the fire (S16):** "I believed it was imperfect." … "Now you're telling me it was *aimed*." … "At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." / Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I did." / "His?" / "No. I read it, after. I did not sign it." … "I would have." / "Yes," Lira said. "You would have."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-368-19. **Ribs (S22):** "That's a line," she said. "That's not yours." / "It's mine now."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-369-20. **Teague's lesson (S21):** "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:370:21. **The court (S23–24):** Vastin: "I stood at a line for forty years," Vastin said, "and told people which side of it they were. I never once asked who drew it." … "This is where they drew it." / Karis: "It's the first one." / Lira: "Right." / Oryn: "Nothing," … "Everything, round it." … "Same as you." / Teague: "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough." … "Field's mine. This isn't field." / at the centre: "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:371:22. **Departures (S24):** Teague: "The thaw's past," / "Noted," / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." / Oryn: "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." / Seln: "Six. Six and no mule. Nothing behind. Nothing beside." / "West," Cael said. / "West," said Brom, and picked up the box. / "Twenty-nine tomorrow," / "Thirty's the month," [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-372-23. **Pike (S2; S17):** "What'd he do?" / "Nothing," Vastin said. "Out here. Nothing yet." / "Then he's nothing yet." And the 297th line: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-373-24. **Vastin's papers (S8):** "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once, so that nobody asks twice."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-374-25. **Oryn at Millrace (S18):** "There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow*. I've spent my life reading flow. Whatever that is, it's not the kind of thing my Path was built for." / "Then it's not mine." … "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." … "Lie still when I say. That's still the term." / "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind."
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-381-- Karis (B7 edition `chapter-57.md:99`; `chapter-60.md:251`): `Three points make a line. Four make an argument.` / `Someone made this pattern.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-382-- Oryn (B7 edition `chapter-58.md:51–55`; `chapter-60.md:215,229`): `Find me at Thornwater.` / `Bring the map.` Her letter: `Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.` / `Six, by letter.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-383-- Hesk's straightedge note (B7 edition `chapter-60.md:67`): `Nineteen. I'm told it's late; the ferry's fault, not mine. Your grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. This one's true to a hair. Mind the shape. — H.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:384:- Teague and Pike (B7 edition `chapter-59.md:199,221–225`): `After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.` / `Noted.` / `I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-385-- Vastin (B6): "I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-386-- The still-place inventory (B7 edition `chapter-60.md:39`): `One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.` Oryn's order (B7 edition `chapter-55.md:289`): `Write it down and stop touching it.` The Tide rule (B7 edition `chapter-60.md:37`): `ask first, every time`. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-387-- The kit's ledger (B7 edition `chapter-52.md:223`): `third site confirmed on bearing`. The audio rule remains `the Bronze from Ardenmere` in spoken inventories. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-402-- **S12:** "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered somewhere, since I'm not the one who keeps the ledger any more." / "It's entered," Log: "Eleventh. Iron Wall, from Vastin, in an alley, while he held a line for us with nothing behind him but the decision to. It's not Brom's — Brom gets harder, this holds. Since my Kindling I've learned to give ground and disappear. Now I've got the opposite in me, from the man who spent forty years being the wall they put in front of people like me. He held it for us instead. I don't have a word for what that is. I wrote it down anyway." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-403-- **S13:** "An instruction *leans*." … "This is a stair." / "The strata lean too." / "Twelfth. His. Lean." / "You did what." / "That's not in the classification system. That's not *supposed* to be possible. That's — " / "No," … "No. I'll not say that one. Not down here. Not to you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-404-- **S14 log lines:** "Hesk sent dividers. Lines are for finding out how far a thing is from another thing. Everything is. I'll enter that as a rule and see what it's worth." / "The promise stands. Not the steps. Not the square." Also: "Out here you count who's owed a seat," … "It's a different ledger."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:405:- **S17 log:** "Karis cracked the grade. The sites are ranked by age and the bearing runs oldest-last — somebody laid them out in order, and the order runs into the deep edge, toward the first one they ever made. Second-tier's the fourth site, the one the Compact fenced. Third-tier's out past it, on the line, quiet for centuries. Teague's crew came after the thaw like he said — ten of us now, and he's still better at this than I am, and the ledger still says so. Two crews, one bearing, and a straightedge my guardian sent me because my grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. Turns out she was right about the line. Turns out the line was already drawn four hundred years ago. We're just the first to follow it to the end." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Also: "Two words," … "Both of them ours." / "Noted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:406:- **S19:** "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / "Noted," / "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times," / win sentence: "The crews had removed the watch's ability to hold the approach by making the only safe retreat a line the watch would not cross and the crews would." / Teague's arm: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint. That's not a healer's opinion. That's a fact about a line." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that now," Log body: "Twelfth—no, count it again—thirteenth. Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend. The Span's the fourth site and the Compact fenced it, years ago by the scale on the iron, and left men on it. They knew. They've always known. The bearing runs through it and keeps going, oldest-last, and the oldest one's out there in the deep edge, quiet since they built the machine. One more site. I've wanted to stand in the middle of it since Karis said *someone made this.* Tomorrow I find out what standing in the middle of the first one feels like."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-407-- **S20 close:** "It's here," Karis said. "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it." / "And it's on the line." / "It's the *end* of the line. Oldest-last. Everything before it was practice, or maintenance, or — I don't have the word. This is the one that's been quiet since before quiet had a name." … "You still want to stand in the middle of it." / "More than I've wanted anything since I was fourteen." / "Why." / "Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died. I want to know what the *oldest* one does to me. I think it's going to tell me something the records can't." [OWNER-pending #57] / He was right. He did not yet know how right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-408-- **S21:** "Behind it. Noted?" / "Noted," (the young one). The far-mouth realization: the line "was not ink".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-409-- **S22 log body:** "Turned the Rune fragment on myself. Cleon said don't. The reading only ever told me the still place was nothing — no flow, no current, a hole where a man should have a middle. The Rune sense says it's not a hole. It says it's *built like something* — like one of those floors with nothing standing on it. Same shape to that fragment as the sites are to Cleon's. I'm not going to write what that might mean, because I don't know, and because the last time I wrote something true in this log a healer made me swear an oath about it. The instruments read wronger for me than they did at Lowmarch. The trend's climbing. My Arbiter's still dark—nothing in me to go quiet, same as always. Tomorrow, the oldest one. I've spent the whole year wanting to stand in the middle of it. I think part of me already knows what I'm going to feel. Nothing. I think I'm going to feel nothing, and I think that's going to be the loudest thing that's ever happened to me." [OWNER-pending #58] ("the whole year", never "the whole book".) [OWNER-pending #58]
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-461-- **Seln teaches nobody anything** before "Draft nothing. Just look." (280th, to Vastin).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-462-- **Seln and Vastin exchange no words** before the 277th long-table doorway.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-463-- **No Iron Wall is shown** before the cut (279th). No Force is shown in Cael's presence before the meadow cart (298th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:464:- **Teague's crew never drills under Vastin's wall** before the pass morning, when the doctrine is told to them once.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:465:- **The tall woman says nothing to any of the six** until her question at the pass. **The broad man says nothing to them** until "Aye" (305th). **The older healer never speaks to them.** **The young one's name is never written** (said once, by the broad man, in the stream-bed). [OWNER-pending #54]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:466:- **"Noted" adoption:** Vastin's first is the 298th (the grade); Teague's first is the 303rd (the crest); Oryn's "Everybody says that now" comes on the 304th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-467-- **Vastin** takes no order without walking it back before Millrace's "Stand there". He does not sit in front of the crew between the cut and the road's last post (281st).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-468-- **Cleon** is above ground with the crew only once (the yard fire). Otherwise he is at noon at his tavern, or on the stair. He takes no notice of Cael until he is told.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-469-- **Oryn's hands** never come off a person with nothing done before the young one (no deaths on her north circuit).
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-479-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-480-## 14. Names
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-481-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:482:**Names pending owner approval: none required.** Every new figure the expansion needs is carried by role: the axe-head hold's factor, the carter at the ice road, the ferryman and his boy, Oryn's route patients (at Oxhollow and unnamed holds), the hold child at the Kindling, the broker's men, and the hood in the tail. This keeps the audio load low in a book whose cast is already heavy with role-names (Teague's crew must stay unnamed by canon). If the author finds a recurring role that needs a name in the audio, it is listed here for approval before drafting, and drafted under the proposed name per the edition's policy (RUN-LEDGER 18:41).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-483-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-484-**Existing names stay exactly as canon has them.** Never "Halcenvane" on the page; use "the academy above Ostrand". The registry collisions are untouched (OWNER-DECISIONS #6). **Audiobook read-through list** (carried): Cleon/Cael (KLEE-on/KAYL; never in one spoken run); Span/Stair; Treswick/Ternhall (keep them out of one spoken inventory); the O-onset stack Oryn/Oxhollow/Ostrand; Pike/Fiske. Places minted by canon only: Treswick, the Deepstacks, the Sunken Span, "the court" (description), the shoulder hold, the cut, the pass. **Do not name new holds** on Oryn's route. Use Oxhollow or Thornwater, or none.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-485-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-487-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-488-## 15. Handoff to Book 9 (series bible: *What Was Lost*)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-489-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:490:Book 9 opens with: the court's centre (no edge; "the same kind of made"); the Rune finding that nobody else knows; the dark Arbiter; the instruments trending wrong; the crack; Vastin unadmitted (Book 9 stages his formal request and the 3–2 vote, with Seln deciding); Oryn's three future holds and "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say."; Teague's "After the next thaw" and his grief; Cleon under Treswick; thirteen fragments; the leaf's copies with the gap drawn; the mule with Oryn; Cael remains nineteen at the Book 9 opening. Do not place or calculate his next birthday until the owner rules the series calendar. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Book 9 owns the tomb in the deepest edge territory, the word "recurrence", the Compact's open fracture (Seln's documents), and the Quieting's first visible spread into a city's outer districts. **Do not pre-pay any of these in Book 8.**
