editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:67:They were going down with two lamps. Karis had filled her brass one to the neck from the can in the left-hand box, and Teague's horn lantern swung in Seln's hand at the head of the file; and by the pair of them the stair was a different place from the one that Cael had gone down at a run. The steps were the grey of the floor, cut out of it and not laid. Every edge was as sharp as on the day that it was made, since no foot had ever worn one.
