editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:119:He went on his knees, with Teague's lantern set down on the stone and pushed ahead of him a foot at a time, and he looked at the dust more than at the thing that lay in it. When he had made the whole circuit he sat back on his heels.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md-120-
