books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-14-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-15-"It's through," Cael said, and drew it, because a fight is drawn before it is fought, and this one had been drawn by the other side first and he wanted his own drawing laid over theirs before anyone walked into it.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-16-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md:17:A hundred strides. The floor a stream-bed, dry, loose stone the size of a fist and a head, that turned under a boot. The west wall a scree slope, the shelf two-thirds up it with the rig on its lip and nine on it, or more. The east wall sheer. The mouth at this end, a cart's width and a half; the far mouth the same. Nowhere in the hundred strides to stand that was not under the shelf. He said it plainly, in the order he had it, and then he said the doctrine, once, to Teague's four, because it was the six's and not theirs and they had not been under it.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-18-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-19-"Vastin puts a wall across the mouth. A plane; not a body — you'll see it and you won't, and you'll know it's there because bolts stop. Everyone behind it. *Everyone.* It doesn't move. It can't. He can't, once it's up. Behind it is behind it and a stride outside it is outside it, and outside it is where a bolt goes." He looked at the young one, because the young one was looking at him as the young look at a thing being explained. "Behind it. Noted?"
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-20-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-21-"Noted," the young one said, and nodded as the young nod, which is with the whole head and none of the rest of them, and Cael entered the nod, and did not know yet that he was going to read the entry again that night and find it the heaviest line on the page.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-22-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md:23:"And then?" the tall woman said. It was the first thing she had said to any of the six in a year.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-24-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-25-"And then Seln goes up," Cael said, "and we find out what nine people do when the ground they built for is under somebody else."
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-26-
--
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-28-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-29-They went in at full light, in the order the pass took them, and he catalogued the order because it was going to be the order the costs came in.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-30-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md:31:Vastin first, with the stick, on the twenty-seventh day of a month, because the wall went where he stood and he had to stand where it went. Cael at his shoulder. Brom at Vastin's other shoulder, bare of everything but himself. Teague and the tall woman. Lira. The broad man on his stick with the crossbow across his back, and the young one beside him, because a man on a stick has a man beside him. Karis with the case and the notebook, and behind her Oryn and the older woman with the cloth bag, with the roll open across Oryn's arm already, because a healer who is going to be needed does not wait to be needed to open the roll. The mule at the mouth with Karis's boxes, tied to a stone, because a mule does not go into a place a man has drawn.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-32-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-33-Seln nowhere. Seln had gone at first light back along the hills' foot to the west, to a place he had looked at from the stream-bed in the dark, and was not on the count, and the count was eleven, and a mule.
