books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-104-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-105-He had not decided that either. He had looked at Seln going over the lip and at the second stack — there was a second; the rig had two, one spent and one still on the shelf's far end, timber-braced, waiting for its own rope, above the place Seln was — and the thirteenth had turned in him toward it as the twelfth had turned toward a still place on a bench, because it was a thing to push against and the thirteenth had been listening for one since a crown, and he had gone up the bare slope after Seln without a word to anyone and was under the second stack with his palm flat on its brace before the ribs had finished telling him what it would cost.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-106-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md:107:He set his feet. He had watched a man do it twice: square, a stride apart, the weight on the balls of them, the whole of himself lined up from the heels through the hips through the shoulder to the flat of the hand as if a straightedge had been laid down him, and he found the line, and it was his — not Teague's; a stride's distance from Teague's; the adjacent thing, the thing that lived beside a Path and was not it — and he pushed.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-108-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md:109:The brace went a body's length. Which was his, from heel to palm, and it was enough: the timber went out from under the stack and the stack went, not down the scree, because he had set the line to take it along the shelf and not off it, but *along*, onto the shelf's far end, where three hoods with crossbows had been standing and were not, because a thing that has been holding a shelf for a season and starts to move is a thing that everyone on the shelf moves away from. The high ground was Seln's. The far end was stone. The near end had the shelf's own stair down it, cut for the team's coming and going, and Teague was on the stair with the tall woman, and Lira was past both of them, because Lira was faster than anyone in the pass and had been since a hall.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-110-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-111-The recoil came back along the line.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-112-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md:113:He had known it would. He had it from a card and from a meadow and from a Span, and he had it now: the cost going back the way the push had gone, through the hand and the arm and the shoulder and down, and stopping — not at the wrist, as Teague's did, because he had not been doing it for twenty years and the line had not yet found its weak place in him — in the ribs. The ribs that had been quiet since a marsh. They said so. They said it once, in the register Oryn used for a finding, which was plainly, and he heard it, and did not sit down, because Seln was on the shelf and the stair had people on it.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-114-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md:115:Teague came up the stair with the other hand.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-116-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md:117:Cael saw it from under the shelf's lip: the man's wrapped arm at his side, useless by a healer's order, and the other hand out, and the frame lined up the other way round, left-handed, awkward, correct, and a hood at the stair's head braced across it with a stave, and Teague's palm on the stave's middle, and the stave and the man behind it a body's length back onto the shelf and down, and the stair open, and the tall woman through it with the spear reversed, the butt and not the point, because nobody on the crew had been told to kill and nobody did. Lira was already on the shelf, with the flat of the blade, at the speed she had.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-118-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-21.md-119-The team broke.
