books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md-110-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md-111-He did not decide to. He entered that afterward, honestly: he had not decided. It had turned as a floor leans that you have stood on for an hour; the eye going along a row whether he told it to or not. Cleon's inside. The lean. He had had it four days and had turned it on nothing since a board, because there had been nothing made to turn it on, on a road; and here, lying still under a turf roof with a healer's current going round a place in him, the twelfth turned, by itself, inward, toward the place, because the place was where everything in him was looking, and the twelfth looked where he looked.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md-112-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md:113:It should have found nothing. That was the card: *made things only; not a river; not a man.* He was a man. The still place was in a man. A record of a thing that was not made would read as what a heap read as, which was nothing with a shape, and he lay and waited for the nothing, and it was the only time in the reading that he was not lying still, and he knew it, and could not stop it any more than he could stop his eye going along six marks in a row.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md-114-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md-115-It did not read as nothing.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md-116-
