books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-02.md-112-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-02.md:113:"The name is in the history. It is a citation, not a person — a reference in a Compact record to a designer, a single individual, that the record does not identify and the Compact has never identified, and the citation's trail runs out of the Compact's own archives and into one it does not hold." He said the next word carefully, as a man says a word he has only read. "Treswick. A pre-Compact archive at a border city on the Line. The trail dead-ends there. I could not follow it from inside. I am not certain anyone can follow it from anywhere, but if it can be followed, it is followed from there, by someone who reads what the Compact never converted."
