books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-12.md:71:He was on the roof of the house on the cut's east side — he had been there, Cael worked out later, since the party had come down the first flight, because Seln went home by a roof when a cut had two ends and he could only watch one — and the landing was under the roof's edge, and the sixth man was on the landing, and a man on a landing in a city at dusk does not look up, because nobody in a city looks up. A cord. That was all it was. A weighted cord, from above, round the sixth man's arm and the rail he stood beside, so that the arm he signalled with was tied to the stair, and then Seln was not on the roof any more and the sixth man was pulling at his own arm in the shadow and saying nothing, because a man tied to a rail does not say the next word; he works at the cord. Nobody died. Nobody was cut. The signal stopped.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-12.md-72-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-12.md-73-And the three at the plane, who had been waiting for the word that told them when to go round by the ring road and take the party from below with the two who were now sitting on the steps, did not get the word, and stood at a plane with their hoods up and a crossbow they had spent and a leader who had gone quiet, and were, for a count of three, six people who did not know what to do.
