books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-12.md-98-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-12.md:99:Seln: back, by the yard gate, with the cache on his back and nothing in his hands and the cord left on the rail because a cord on a rail was a thing that could be found and a man could not, and he came up the steps and looked at the two staves and the bolt and said, "They'll go to ground and think. They know where we sleep now. They knew before, but now they know we know." He looked at the plane's place, where the air had stopped being stone. "They came for a declaration. They got a wall and a rock. They don't know what to make of that, and they'll want to."
