books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md:47:That was all of it. That was what Oryn had taught him on a table in the sun: *listening with my hands to how you're built* — but the listening was for flow, for the thing that moved through the architecture, for where it pooled and broke and ran wrong. It was an instrument for movement. It was the best instrument for movement he had ever seen, and it had been built by a Path whose whole name was *current*, and it could no more read a thing that did not move than a cord could measure a thing that had no length.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-48-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md:49:He had been putting a cord on a stone and writing down *no length*.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-50-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-51-He sat with that. The river ran below him. The city stood across it with its three walls and its gates and the thing on its crown that he was not looking at, and he sat against a post with his hands on his knees and understood, plainly, that four readings had told him exactly one true thing about the still place, which was that it was not a matter of flow, and that he had been reading that one true thing as *nothing* for six months because the instrument had no other word for it.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-52-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md:53:He tested it, because a finding that was not tested was a guess wearing a finding's coat, and he had heard that said at a slab two days ago and had agreed with it. He put the hands back where the form put them, the one on the sternum and the other under his back against the post, and ran the reading a fifth time — not to the middle; to the ten — and asked it, in the only way it could be asked, what it could tell him about a thing that did not move, and it told him what it had told him four times: the ten went round; the going-round was real; the thing they went round was, to an instrument for current, a place where the current was not. A cord on a stone. He took the hands off. Five readings, one finding, and the finding was about the cord.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-54-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-55-You cannot measure a stillness with a thing that only feels movement.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-56-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md:57:He did not have another instrument. He had ten things that were not a Path and every one of them was a thing that moved, or held, or burned, or cut, and not one of them was for reading a thing that did none of those. He had a cord that read everyone but him and two brass edges that read a hair off in his hands and a healer on a north track since first light who had had her hands in him twice and been told the rest, and got a floor, and a man across a river who, Karis said, read how things were built.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-58-
