books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md:83:"That's all of it. That's every room we were ever in. They built a thing to read people, and you were the part that read, and I was the part it couldn't." He turned it over once. "And now there's no thing. There's a road. There's you with a stick and me with a satchel and a cord that reads a hair wrong in my hands, and nobody on this road is going to read either of us, because the only instrument on it is across a river, and I've promised a healer I won't go near it."
