books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-10-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-11-Karis sat down. She sat where she sat at a source — the near side, the lamp to her left, the notebook flat, the pencil in the hand that did not turn pages — and she put both hands on the table, and looked at the pack, and did not look at Vastin at all, which was, Cael thought, the greatest courtesy she had ever paid anyone.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-12-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:13:"Three things," Vastin said. "In the order I decided on the road. I'll tell you the order and then I'll keep to it. First the records. Then the page. Then the thing in the records that I could not get past, which is the reason for the other two, and which I would have told you first if I were a different kind of man."
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-14-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-15-"You're not," Karis said.
