books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-54-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-55-Vastin took it from inside his coat, not from the flat, because it had never been in the flat: a single sheet, folded twice, in the ordinary paper the Compact used for the ordinary business of a day, and the hand on it was his own — square, upright, a hand made for filling boxes on forms — and there were four lines on it.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-56-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:57:He set it apart. He set it on the table's bare end, past the sixth row, and did not slide it toward Karis, and did not look at Cael, and Cael understood that the setting-apart was part of the order the man had decided on the road: the records were a stack; this was a page; a stack could be sorted and a page could only be read.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-58-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:59:"I copied it from a record older than the section it was filed in," Vastin said. "The classified history is not one history. It is an office's habit, kept for a long time, of putting a thing on a shelf it does not want read, and the shelf is older than the office. The oldest things on it are not Compact records at all. They are what the Compact found when it built the office, and did not throw away, because throwing a thing away is a decision and filing it is not. This was on the oldest shelf. It is a reference — a line in a longer record, citing another record that the Compact does not hold — and it is the only line in all the classified history that names a designer."
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-60-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-61-"Names," Karis said.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-62-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:63:"Cites. There is no name. There is a word the record uses for him, which I have copied as it was written, and there is the place where the record it cites is said to be kept, which I have copied as it was written, and there is nothing else, because there was nothing else. I did not copy the rest of the line. The rest of the line is a clerk's hand telling a later clerk where a shelf was."
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-64-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-65-Karis reached across the sixth row and took the page.
