books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-89-The third thing.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-90-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md:91:Vastin did not take it out of anything. It was already on the table. It had been on the table since the first row went down, because it was in the records, and he had known where, and had let Karis lay it in its place among the survey sheets and had waited for her to be done sorting before he said which sheet it was, because that, too, was the order.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-92-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-03.md-93-"The sheet at the end of the second row," he said. "Not a survey. The office filed it with the surveys because the office did not know what else to file it with. Read the last line."
