books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-13.md-48-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-13.md-49-He did not use it. He had not used the eleventh either. He stood with the lamp in his hand and the twelfth thing in him and did not turn it on anything but the sheet it had come off, because a thing that had come to him from a man working in front of him was a thing he owed the man the knowing of before he owed himself the using, and because there was one place in him he was not going to turn it, and he knew that place, and he had been told by a healer not to touch it, and had been told by this man, on the third day down, that the instrument did not work on a man, and he was going to find out which of those two things was true by asking neither of them tonight.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-13.md-50-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-13.md:51:He held the lamp. Cleon turned his head a finger's width, and the light was there, and Karis, across the table, who had watched him not turn the twelfth thing on anything, looked at him once, as she had looked at him on a road with a cord in his hand, and said nothing, and wrote nothing, because it was not hers to enter and she knew whose it was.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-13.md-52-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-13.md-53-The rest of the day was the rest of a day in the chamber, and he catalogued it because a day in which a man had come to own a twelfth thing should be catalogued as an ordinary day, so that the twelfth thing would not think itself all of it. Cleon and Karis at the table with the fourth row and the fifth and the board, the pencil going now, Karis's, in the notebook, faster than he had seen it go since a marsh. Brom on the first box with the foot out and the good shoulder held, held like a thing he had used wrong and does not intend to use again for a while. Lira standing, then sitting on the third box, then standing, because a room with three galleries going off it into the dark was a room she did not sit in for long. Vastin on the knee, beside the case, not sitting, being nobody a little better than the day before, which Cael measured by the number of times the man's hand moved toward the lamp and stopped: four, on the fourth day; two, today. And the twelfth thing in him, with nothing to do, leaning at every mark on every sheet on the table whether he asked it to or not, so that the chamber was full of small directions he had not had yesterday and could not now stop having, and he found that a made room was a thing that pointed, everywhere, at what its makers had wanted next, and that he was going to have to learn not to look, as he had learned not to look at a light on a hill.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-13.md-54-
