books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-29-"Or that." She did not look up. "The rows don't say which way's first. Cleon said an instruction leans toward where it's going. I can't tell you whether the going was east or the coming was west. I can tell you the rows agree with the line, and the line agrees with the ages, and the ages run east."
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-30-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md:31:She laid the index against the records, then, and the records against the walls, and it was the work of an hour and he watched the whole hour and did not enter any of it, because it was a reconciliation and a reconciliation was one entry, at the end, when the columns agreed.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-32-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-33-They agreed. The dead man's grades in the kit's index were the office's marks on the sheets, first and second and third, and the office's dates by first sheet were the ages the walls' rows leaned along, and the fourth site's radius on the carter's sheet was the fourth site's radius on the office's, twice the others, and the stake count on the iron was the stake count in the ledger, and a distance from a hold on the office's sheet with the stroke and two bars was the distance she walked the dividers across from that hold, and the point came down where it had come down at Lowmarch, past the fourth, on the line, in the straightedge's shadow.
