books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-127-She had the reconciled sheet flat on the blanket's last fold, with the four circles and the line and the fifth circle, thumbnail-sized, past the hills, and the straightedge from Denvash laid along the line because he had laid it there, and the edge touched the fifth circle as it touched the other four, without a hair of daylight, dead along, and neither of them said anything about that, because they had said everything about that there was to say at a landing in the snow.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md-128-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-20.md:129:"It's here," Karis said. "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it."
