books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-14.md-12-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-14.md-13-He did not open it at once. He catalogued the five first, because a thing was about to be opened and he wanted the room from before, as he had wanted a back room from before a pack was opened: Brom at the table's end with the foot up on the empty chair, which was what an empty chair was for; Lira across from him with her two hands on the wood, the left one open, because she opened it now without thinking, which was all that twenty-seven days had done; Seln at the door end, facing the street door, because a street door in a city where a team knew where they slept was a thing somebody faced; and Vastin, on the knee, at the table's side, with the stick against the bench and his hands on his knees, at a crew's table on a working day for a thing that was not work, and not knowing what the thing was, and not asking.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-14.md-14-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-14.md:15:He pulled the cord. It came undone with one pull.
