editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:17:Brom set the kit on the table. Its case lay there in tarred canvas, with the strap coiled on the lid; inside were a cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke and the bar and a bright turned point, and a mallet. The stake had never been driven. Beside it Karis put a dead man's ledger, shut. The three boxes stood against the warm wall, and each of them had one leaf in it that was the same as its fellows.
