books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-22.md-72-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-22.md:73:That was the first word, and it was not a word he chose; it was the word the shape was nearest, and he let it stand because he had no better one and because a cataloguer enters the nearest word and marks it *nearest*. Not a hole. A hole was what the tenth had found, because the tenth was for current and a place with no current is a hole to it, as a room with no light is dark to an eye. This was not that. This had *structure*. It went a way. It had a thing that bore and a thing that was borne, and rows, and the rows leaned, and the lean was the lean of the floors — the same lean; the one he had seen go along six marks on a board and along a Span's piers toward the east — and it was not a heap and it was not nothing and it was not a man's, because a man, Cleon said, did not read, and this read.
