books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md-135-She said it plainly, in the register, as she said every finding, and she said it looking at him and not at the ford, which was not the register and was the other thing.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md-136-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md:137:"There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow*. I've spent my life reading flow. Whatever that is, it's not the kind of thing my Path was built for."
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md-138-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-18.md-139-He said, "Noted," because it was the word, and because it was true, and because it was the same finding she had given him at a marsh with less certainty and had now given him with all of it, and a finding that has been made certain is a different entry from one that has been made.
