books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-06.md-49-That was different. That was the register she kept for a finding she was afraid of, which he had heard three times in his life, and he sat up.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-06.md-50-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-06.md:51:"You're walking into a city with a station in it." She was looking at him now, and only him, across the fire, and the five of them let her, because it was hers. "An Arbiter station. At the top of the tiers, with a light on it. I've never seen one from the inside and I never want to, but I know what it's for, because I was certified under one: it's the thing that reads a practitioner. It's the instrument. It's the biggest instrument on the continent, and there's one in every city, and it reads everyone who walks up its steps, and I have had my hands on you four times and got nothing three times and the fourth time a thing I still can't name, and then a cord told me the same, and I don't know what you are, and I'm a healer, and there is one rule a healer learns before she learns to set a bone." She stopped. She made herself say the next thing slowly. "You do not walk a body you can't read toward the one instrument on the continent that reads bodies. Not because I know what it'd do. Because I don't. I don't know what it'd do to you and I don't know what you'd do to it, and a healer who doesn't know what a thing will do keeps her patient away from the thing. That's the whole of medicine. That's the rule under all the other rules."
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-06.md-52-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-06.md-53-"I'm not going near it," Cael said.
--
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-93-The river ran. Lira, up the road, was standing with her two hands at her sides looking at the walls, and Brom was sitting with the foot up, and Karis was reading the bluff, and Seln was somewhere.
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-94-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md:95:"I'll tell you one," he said. "Because you told me one and that's the only exchange rate I know." He looked at his own hands. "I've a thing in the middle of me that I've been reading for six months with an instrument that can't read it. I found that out just now, against that post. Every reading I've ever run on it came back nothing and I wrote *nothing* down four times, and it wasn't nothing; it was the tool. I've been putting a cord on a stone." He was quiet. "Nobody has that. Not Karis. Not the healer. Not the file. You're the first person I've said it to, and I've said it to you because you've no file to put it in."
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-96-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-07.md-97-Vastin took that. Cael watched him take it — the stillness, the hands on the stick — and watched him not draft anything, which was a thing he had been taught at a spring and was keeping.
