books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-04.md-148-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-04.md:149:Himself: the burst's bill, which he knew the price of to the copper — breath, gone; the ten frameworks knocking together in him like a cart on a bad road, which would last the day; the ribs, which had been quiet since the marsh and were quiet still, which he noted, because a thing that stayed quiet was a thing you wrote down. The still place at the middle of them, untouched, unmoved, going around nothing. He did not read it. He had not been asked to.
