books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-01.md:201:Oryn said nothing to that, which was not agreement, and was not the other thing. It was the kind of nothing that a healer says when a patient she cannot read is about to walk toward the one place on the continent a healer's whole training says to keep an unreadable body away from, and has not asked her, and she has not decided what she would say if he did. Cael saw it. He did not answer it. It was hers, and she would say it when she said it, and the ferry had not run.
