+# PLAN / CANON / PROTECTED-TEXT AUDIT — Movement 1
+
+## Verdict
+
+**RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES — manuscript scope: chapters 1–6 may close after the fourteen exact fixes below.** No scene-order or structural rewrite is required. The surviving draft keeps the locked Book 7 seam, the movement beats, the calendar, the twenty-seven-to-twenty-nine deployment arithmetic, and all sequence locks. The required manuscript work is confined to four expected Tier-B restorations and their joins, five corrections to the kit cord's length, one no-count-since-Kindling correction, and the protected `Lie still` attribution (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:219`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:65`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:9-13,25,47,107`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:119,133,245-251`).
+
+**Plan/ledger follow-up outside this audit's write authority is required before the affected later movements:** amend Teague's spear to a man; amend Teague's literacy; amend Lira's “first ask” wording; preserve the Book 7 distribution of the stroke-and-bar; change the court's `159 cords`; and clarify that Karis builds the costly proposition on the 263rd but first says *west* in the restored 268th speech (`BOOK_MAP.md:88,90,110,114,153,193,203-216,326,459,465`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:19,89`). Book 7 is text-locked and hash-bound, so those conflicts should be repaired forward in Book 8 unless the owner expressly orders a Book 7 re-bind (`book-07-void-roads/DIRECTOR_CUT_READY.md:3-12,20-25,37-39`).
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+### Seam result
+
+The movement preserves the locked Book 7 end state:
+
+- **Date and company.** Book 7 ends on day 131 with five people and the brown mule at Lowmarch (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:219-239`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:121-147`). Book 8 opens later that morning with the same five and mule (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:3-9`); Oryn is absent at Thornwater until the day-265/266 visit and joins them at Lowmarch on day 268 (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:3,61-79,215`). Teague's four practitioners plus the older healer remain the other five at the upper inn (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:251`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:157-223`).
+- **Bodies.** Lira enters with her left arm slung and inert, right ankle taped and unmended, and Oryn's crossbow with its single bolt (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:225-235`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:57-59,109`; `manuscript/chapter-02.md:7`). Brom's right shoulder remains twice mended and held in four yards of webbing (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:229-231`; `manuscript/chapter-02.md:7,181-183`). Cael's ribs remain quiet (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:31-41`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:15-19`). At movement end Lira has released her own sling and Oryn has mended the ankle, while Brom's shoulder remains in the older healer's knot (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:83-105,111-143`).
+- **Counts and money.** Book 7 closes at ten fragments, twenty-seven deployments, ninety-six living marks, nine board lines, and eleventh on the cloth (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:11,31-39`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:161-177,211-215`). Book 8 enters with precisely those figures (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:15,49,91`) and the purse reconciles `96 - 20 + 40 + 5 - 3 = 118` (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:235-243`; `manuscript/chapter-02.md:265-281`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:215-219`). The fence and roof raise Pike's book to eleven lines while the cloth remains eleventh (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:279-283`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:217,281-283`).
+- **Archive objects.** The tarred case, cord, unused stake 32, mallet, dead man's ledger, fifty-two sheets, map, and two brass edges enter intact (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:15-27,59-73`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:63-73,119-125`). The draft keeps stake 32 undriven (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:65-69`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:259`), opens the ledger only after the ice road (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:253-281`), and owns the planned first hair of error on day 168 (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:57-113`), after Book 7 showed both edges true in Cael's hand (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:237-245`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:48`).
+- **Letters, animals, and debts.** Hesk's and Vell's letters are west; Ephram's remains due on the first boat; the ferryman's sixty yards of four-strand rope remains owed (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:75-91`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:49`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:213-229`). The movement adds one reed hurdle debt through a logged trial (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:265-299`). The brown mule remains with the crew and earns a three-mark cold-term shed fee (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:9,229-235`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:217-219,281`); Oryn's grey jenny remains at Thornwater by implication and is not contradicted (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:99-147`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:61-77`).
+- **The Quieting and knowledge.** The fourth site remains unnamed, unentered, untouched, and untested at 440 yards and two strides; Oryn is told its description and measurement without seeing or touching it (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:145-173,185-225`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:163-187`). Cael does not read or touch the still place (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:283-297`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:283-285`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:201`). The label was said to Oryn, while the description was told to the other four, exactly as the seam requires (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:245-289`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-57.md:191-209`).
+- **Debt direction.** Cael's debt to Oryn was paid, not forgiven: Oryn says “It's paid,” while the other matter “was never a debt” and still stands (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:235-289`). Book 8 does not reopen or reverse that debt; its proposed Millrace reading remains a new future event (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:193-209`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:93,105`).
+
+No contradiction remains in the current movement's people, bodies, money, archive inventory, fragment inventory, fourth-site state, or knowledge state after the fixes below. The sole physical-object contradiction in the draft is the kit cord's proposed twenty-five-stride length (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:9-13`), against the source's twenty-stride cord (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-01.md:31`) and Book 7's sixty-two-cord/two-hundred-and-twenty-yard geometry (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-57.md:13`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-52.md:295`). Fixes 3–7 restore four five-stride intervals and keep the yard at forty-two strides.
+
+## 2. Movement plan and every owner flag
+
+### Beats, order, and withheld material
+
+Every packet beat is present in the required order: cold-stay pricing on day 133 (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:197-243`); fence and shale-backs on days 138–146 (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:3-47,51-229,233-283`); silent-yard learning beginning day 148 and recurring on days 158 and 190 (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:3-149`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:3-65`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:219-231`); the day-161 ice road (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:69-243`); the day-168 anomaly (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:3-113`); Karis's private costly proposition on day 263 (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:259-281`); Thornwater on days 265–266 (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:3-209`); and the six-person case and closing log on days 268–270 (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:215-289`).
+
+All withheld items survive. Oryn does not read Cael (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:193-201`); Seln teaches nobody (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:95-99`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:253`); the tall one, broad man, and older healer never speak to the five (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:49-85,157-223`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:3-65`); no Iron Wall or Vastin appears; no Force is shown in Cael's presence (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:157-171`); Karis cannot read the index or identify its grade (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:263-281`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:161-195`); *Treswick* and *Deepstacks* first occur in speech at the day-268 table (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:215,243-253`); Cleon is not named; the anomaly remains deniable and theory-free (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:93-113,145-155`); nobody says who made the pattern or why; and the still place is neither read nor touched (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:189-201`).
+
+### Owner flags — rulings
+
+1. **Teague's spear — AMEND BOOK 8 PLAN, KEEP BOOK 7.** Book 7's complete gendered references are: `chapter-25.md:85` (“a man with a spear”); `chapter-51.md:357` (“He,” “a man”); `chapter-52.md:45` (“a tall man,” “he”); `chapter-52.md:335` (“a tall man”); and `chapter-52.md:337` (“He,” “the man,” “his spear”). Book 8's plan says woman at `BOOK_MAP.md:88,110,114,153,326,465`; §10 contains no gendered reference to the spear (`BOOK_MAP.md:343-405`); and the entry ledger repeats “tall spear woman” (`STATE_LEDGER.md:19`). The historical source's complete gendered references are `chapter-02.md:59`; `chapter-17.md:79,99,123,179`; `chapter-18.md:21,47,169`; `chapter-19.md:47,97,117`; `chapter-21.md:23,31,109,117,133`; `chapter-22.md:5,9`; `chapter-23.md:21,41,73,97`; and `chapter-24.md:109`, all woman/feminine. The present movement correctly avoids deciding it in prose (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:251`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:11,49-85`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:43-63`). Because Book 7 is locked and a change invalidates its hash (`book-07-void-roads/DIRECTOR_CUT_READY.md:20-25`), amend Book 8's plan, ledger, later protected-source staging, and later packets from *tall woman/she/her* to *tall man/he/him*; do not re-bind Book 7 for a role whose current movement already works gender-neutral.
+2. **Teague reads — AMEND BOOK 8 PLAN.** Locked Book 7 has Pike say, “He read that slip yesterday. Read it twice” (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-25.md:43`), then directly shows Teague read a paper “from the first word to the seal” and start again (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-25.md:75-79`). Book 8's cutaway rule says he does not read (`BOOK_MAP.md:197`), and the historical source repeats that error (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-17.md:133,171`; `chapter-24.md:109`). The current prose is correctly neutral: he cannot read a sheet **from another house in the dark**, but knows its stable contents (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:223`). Amend the plan to “he can read; he cannot see the sheet from here and does not need to.”
+3. **Lira's first ask — AMEND PLAN/LEDGER WORDING, KEEP MANUSCRIPT.** Locked Book 7 shows Lira ask Oryn, “Can you mend it?” and “Will you?” on the mountain (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-21.md:165-177`), then states she had asked once (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-21.md:183-185`). Thus “first ask since Norhold” is false (`BOOK_MAP.md:459`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:89`). The draft gives the exact truth: she asked once on the mountain and asked nobody for anything afterward until Thornwater (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:111-115`). Amend plan and ledger to that wording.
+4. **Stroke and bar — AMEND BOOK 8 PLAN, KEEP BOOK 7 AND CURRENT PROSE.** Stake 31 has number/stamp but no stroke-and-bar (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-28.md:119-127`; `chapter-43.md:13`); the newer 32 and unused kit stake 32 have it (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-48.md:203-211`; `chapter-52.md:139-147`); stake 33 has nothing beneath the number (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md:145-153`); and the repeated 34 cordon carries it (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:165-177`). The current Karis window preserves exactly that distribution (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:161-175`). Amend the future spine claim that the mark is on all four sites; later records may show the grade on survey sheets, but the four field stakes do not.
+5. **Cord length — AMEND CURRENT CORD SCENE AND FUTURE COURT COUNT.** The kit cord is twenty strides, knotted every five (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-01.md:31`), while locked Book 7's circle works out near twenty-two yards per cord (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-57.md:13`; `chapter-52.md:295`). Fixes 3–7 make one length four five-stride intervals. For the court, retain the converted diameter “about 1,107 yards” but change `159 cords` to **about fifty cords** (`BOOK_MAP.md:36,90,135`): 159 cords at Book 7's scale would be roughly 3,500 yards. The historical 1,012-metre/159-cord pairing is internally incompatible with the locked cord and is reviewer-only, not edition canon (`universe/UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:238-239`; `books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-23.md:43`).
+6. **Deployment count — KEEP 29.** Book 7 defines a trial as not a use and excludes the Hall Anchor trial and self-readings while closing at 27 (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md:383-389`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:299-301`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:78,83`). The calf read solves a trapped living body and is explicitly counted as deployment 28 (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:173-229`); the river-ice read solves the rescue and is explicitly “In earnest,” producing 29 (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:101-199,239-243`). Shed/meadow work remains “Trials. Not counted,” Anchor stays at two counted uses, Shadow stays twice and sealed, and no Tide use occurs (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:293-305`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:201-217`). The plan fixes only the **entry** count at 27, not a cold-term exit count (`BOOK_MAP.md:259`).
+7. **Four markers — RESTORE.** Full rulings and speakers are in §5; fixes 1, 8, 10, and 14 replace the four marker lines (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:219`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:107`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:133,251`).
+8. **Cutaways and vocabulary — ACCEPT; WATCH CUMULATIVE TARGET.** Teague is 1,538 words and Karis about 1,905, total 3,445 against approximate guidance of 4,500 (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:39`); all required content is present (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:157-231`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:117-195`). The strict progression count is 58 per 10k against the first-third target of about 82 (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:41`; `BOOK_MAP.md:274-282`), but the reader is nevertheless taught all ten costs/limits and the kit procedure (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:75-99,271-291`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:235-305`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:199-217`). Do not pad this movement; make Movements 2–3 carry the cumulative first-third shortfall.
+9. **Months — KEEP.** Generic *month* is allowed, no month length is stated, and “Five months and twenty days.” stands verbatim and unglossed (`OWNER-DECISIONS.md:175-180`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:57,235-243`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:83-89`).
