editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:359:- **Bodies** [corrected at close, 2026-10-11: an earlier version of this bullet wrongly said Cael's calf was mended; "the leg" the packet means is LIRA'S]: **Lira's right tibia, broken on the 78th, was set and MENDED by Oryn on the 80th** (straight and new; to walk within the week; not to be run on for a month). **Lira's right ANKLE is NOT mended** ("a tape and a season"); her right boot is under the plate and she is barefoot on that side, taped, through day 84. **Cael:** three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break (whole on the 99th by Oryn's rule). **His calf (the ford bite) is NOT mended by anyone: it is cloth-bound and healing on its own.** Karis emptied by the lattice. Exact states in the author's section below, as corrected after repair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:362:- **Withheld and intact:** nobody mentions quiet ground; of Oryn's seven holds only Oxhollow and Thornwater are named; no new names; "nineteen" does not appear.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:399:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst, day 53). Nothing was used on the mountain or since: Anchor, Compression, the Iron read, Wind and Storm all offered and were refused; Shadow sealed. **Three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped with five bands on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break, and Oryn means to lift the tape herself.** Left calf opened along the old bite on the 78th, bound in Oryn's linen, not mended. No log entries for the 78th and 79th. He has been read three times by a healer (the 80th, and twice on the 84th) and has answered three questions truly: his hurts knit in the right places; faster than other people's; no healer has ever got anything from him. He has not asked Oryn south. He has not answered Hesk's letter. Teague has spoken to him and he has said one word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:409:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, said by herself. She knows that she cannot read Cael, by surface reading, hurt or whole, and that his ribs knit "with nothing doing it"; she knows nothing of fragments and has no theory. She has promised him the long reading "when you're not broken". **Her sum (her window, the 92nd):** whole on the 99th by the rule, though her hands say sooner; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; her Thornwater stop ends on the 95th; she means to work four days more at Thornwater's table and has put one day on the route, for the reading. She is five days behind her round. She has mended six times on the page: Lira's leg and Brom's wrist (80th); a scald, a foot and a collarbone (84th); and, in her window, a shoulder at two mendings' cost (86th). She keeps no record. She told Teague on the hill only that she was late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:411:**Teague.** At Oxhollow's ford at dusk on the 84th he said his four things and crossed. He knows: no cart; a wrist in a healer's cuff; the girl's foot strapped; the small one asleep sitting up; the boy's ribs taped; that the mountain came down and all five came off it, mostly on their feet; that the keeper paid seventy for a no. **He knows that the healer was late to the upper hold on the 81st, where he had waited a day for the bow's hip, and he does not know why; he has not connected it with the five.** He does not know what Cael is. He and his three (the spear, the bow, the boy) and two mules are a day ahead on the road south.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:417:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. Oryn knows that a healer's hands cannot read him and that he heals fast; she has been told nothing. Oxhollow's keeper knows that a Path used under the shale-backs brings the hill down, as derived. **Nobody has mentioned quiet ground.** Oryn's other holds are unnamed; Thornwater and Oxhollow are the only two named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:422:Movement 4 already carries the dusk-of-84 location, 116 in hand / six owed, taped ribs, bound calf, new leg, missing right boot, Oryn north, Teague south, nine days to Thornwater, and the three boxes (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:18-20`). It must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:428:- Cael's three left-low ribs were broken day 78 and received five bands on day 81, to be lifted on day 99 by Oryn if possible; his reopened calf is only cloth-bound. His nine fragments are held, Shadow remains sealed, and deployment since the Line is one (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:121-155`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:3-45`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-333`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:448:- **Bodies** as the closed Movement 3 left them, advanced by days: Lira's tibia mended and not to be run on; her ankle NOT mended; Cael's ribs taped (whole on the 99th); his calf bound; Karis recovering. Oryn changed her ch22 plan at Thornwater's gate on the 93rd and walked the Fallow road.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:509:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. All six know what quiet ground does to a live Arbiter, to the stride, and that a healer's hands stop there. The party knows that the registry's iron stands on the line, numbered thirty-one, some five years old; that no instruments are at the site; that hounds den under the floor. **Nobody but Cael knows that anything answers inside.** Pike, Teague, the clerk and the holds know only that five people took a paper.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:519:- **Bodies at dusk:** Cael's ribs remain taped until day 99 and his calf remains bound, not mended; Lira's tibia is new and barred from running until about day 110, her ankle remains unmended/taped, and she has drawn her knife; Brom's wrist is sound; Karis is three parts full; Seln is unmarked; Oryn cannot read or mend inside (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:23-43,181-233`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:207-215,237`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:169-179`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:537:- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTEEN.** One at the ford (day 53) and twelve in the Ring on the night of the 96th, each priced and billed in the night log: Iron read; Shadow (once, ten strides); Wind; Pressure; Ember (one point on the knife's tip); Blade (an edge on Lira's knife); Anchor (perception only — a deliberate release counts); Storm lanes one, two and three (ten / ten / twelve counts; the body read lost while the air is held); Wind a second time; Compression at contact, late. The two noon tests of the 96th are left out of the number, unexplained. All capability rules held.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:542:- **Bodies:** Lira — right ankle gone a third time; forearm bitten and held, mended by Oryn outside the line (one mending "the size of two"), arm in a sling, walking flat-footed on Oryn's order; tibia mended earlier. Karis — throat, mended. Brom — ONE hand, the pads of FOUR fingers cut by the string, mended, four dark lines; no string until the 100th. Cael — the calf opened again on a stone (bound, closing by itself, not mended); left forearm (Compression's bill); ribs whole on the 99th. Oryn spent "three in two days… that's a route".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:560:- **What the reading is like from under it (flag):** it goes along the length of a person and returns to her other hand, at the pace she walks, favouring the right by a hair. He can tell where she is. As she passes: Wind turns over and settles; his palm warms; Compression does nothing; the read wishes to open; the ninth draws itself in small, unasked; the heaviest lies quiet. She says "You're helping." when his neck hardens.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:603:- **Bodies:** Lira's left arm remains slung and under the no-hold/no-strike/no-catch order; her right ankle is unmended and she must walk flat; her mended tibia is not to be run on until about day 110 (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:101-125`; `manuscript/chapter-35.md:63-69,155-215`). Cael's ribs and calf are whole, but the left forearm has sensation only as far as the wrist on day 99 (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:265-329`). Karis has only rough single words (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:9`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:635:- **The listening (flag):** his own current at the edge of every thought, quick and slow; the nine by sound (Wind, dry grass going over; the read, a millstone through a floor; Ember, a wick ticking; Pressure, a bellows; Compression, hemp under load; Anchor, one held note; Blade, a wet finger on a glass; Shadow, a hush that drops the others; Storm, a sea turning over). It cannot be refused, since it asks for nothing. Three nights. Asked on the 101st where it is loudest, he answers at the breastbone: it is not louder there, it is nearer (the protected line).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:646:- **Why "the Quieting" (flag):** *quiet ground* is a carter's word for where; she wants the word for what happens; *the quiet* sits, *sleep* claims a will, *silencing* claims a voice; hers is made from a verb, takes a place after it, and claims only that it is one thing. **It is for the box:** asked whether it should go to Pike, she says that he and the carters have a word of their own and have kept alive by it, and that she will not hear hers in a meadow before she knows whether it is right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:664:**Cael.** **Nineteen** since the middle of the meal on the 102nd. **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth (Tide-adjacent) has been used on himself only: three days of listening, idle by the third night; one self-reading on the night of the 102nd. He has found **a place near the middle of himself that does not flow**, which all ten go round; he knows where it is, that nothing moves in it, and that none goes through; he has not named it, has not gone back to it, and has told nobody what it is. He has told Lira and then the six that there is a thing, and that it is the healer's to hear first. The three standing words are retired; the log reads *Patience is over; observation begins.* **Deployment since the Line: thirteen**; eleven leans of Wind in the yard on the 101st are logged as practice outside the number. Shadow unused; it lifts at dusk and is refused. Body whole: ribs, calf; the left forearm's feeling back to the knuckles on the 100th, a yellow mark. He has said to Oryn that it was wrong; he has not been forgiven. **He owes her:** three readings of himself on three different days, and then all of it at once; he does not know what she would have said at the door and never will; the size of the rest is hers. **The rule** is in his book in his hand, with her note under it. He has told the six that he knew at noon on the 96th. He holds a hypothesis that he has not written. Three letters still unanswered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:707:- **Deployment since the Line: TWENTY-THREE.** Fourteen is Tide on Oryn on the 113th (one sitting, short count then a minute of the long, counted as one). Fifteen to twenty-three are on the 114th: Anchor, looking, at the two stakes (dawn); then at dusk Shadow (once); the read, in the ground; Anchor, looking, for the knot (absent at fourteen feet, faint at twelve, sure at ten); Anchor, the unbinding, palm on the knot (no reach, rate or price assigned); Wind, one burst; Storm, one lane up the old rut; Compression at contact; Ember, one point on the knife. Nothing was used inside the line in sight of the rim; Tide was used on nobody inside any line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:788:- **Bills and bodies:** Cael's right forearm bends but carries Compression's blow, and his left palm is taped with an unmended weal; Lira's reopened marks are shut and the sling is shorter, but the no-hold order and taped/unmended ankle stand; Brom's right arm is bound after one shoulder mending and must not be used until Oryn says (51:123–163; 52:5,75).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:804:- **Deployment since the Line: TWENTY-SEVEN at book end.** Twenty-three after the Stair; then at the Hall on the 119th the read under water (24), Compression taken standing (25), an Anchor point laid by hand in the breach and held (26); and on the 120th Tide on Oryn, asked and granted, one sitting (27). The Anchor point set as a trial on the 118th is NOT counted ("I'll not call a trial a use"), which agrees with the protected inventory: Anchor used twice this year, once each way (the Stair's unbinding; the Hall's holding). Self-readings are not counted. **Shadow was not used**; it has been used exactly twice in the book and remains sealed; Oryn does not know Seln is its source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:811:- **Bodies:** Lira's left arm slung and holding nothing, her right ankle never mended; her order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"); Oryn's crossbow is with Lira with ONE bolt left. Brom's shoulder opened, was mended a second time and is BOUND, not mended a third ("It will not hold three times this season"). Cael's three old ribs took Compression again (ten days; quiet on the 129th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:827:- **Compression in the Hall:** the strike goes "through the bones of his legs, and his hips, and up his back and down again, and out through both heels into the ledge"; the tipping plate is driven flat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:834:- **Teague's healer (flag; unnamed):** "sixty, or near it, as lean as a rake", grey hair knotted under a cap, a much-mended satchel, a staff that she does not lean on; no Path that mends ("I've no Path that knits"); forty cold terms of binding; with the crew for nine, since "a ford with a carter's leg in it"; she spends the dry months at her daughter's hold up the north water and comes down at the first hard frost. She carries a splinting board, four yards of webbing and raw wool. **The binding:** a pad under the arm; webbing round the chest, over the point of the shoulder and back beneath the elbow, three times, with "a drover's" turn (under, and back on itself) that keeps the weight on the ribs and off the joint. Oryn asks to be shown it twice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:851:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten confirmed fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: twenty-seven** (the ford 1; the Ring 12; Oryn on the ridge 1; the Stair 9; the Hall 3; Oryn at the marsh 1). The trial point at the Hall's kerb on the 118th is logged and not counted. Shadow used twice in all and shut. Anchor: looked three times; unbound once (the Stair); a point set twice, of which one is the uncounted trial and one held the breach. Tide: Oryn twice, each time by her leave; himself three times (102, 119, 120); nobody else; never inside a line. **The still place:** his old log label, now a location under the breastbone, read three times; nothing moves in it; all ten go round it and none through; they do not pile against it; not the Quiet; not a fragment; told to Oryn at once and in order on the 120th, and to the other four in three sentences on the 121st; he has been told to write it down and stop touching it, and has not touched it since. Body: ribs quiet since the morning of the 129th; right forearm and left palm no longer remarked; calf a closed seam. Hesk's satchel: the log (the entries of the 118th, 119th, 120th, the fork, the crest, and the inventory of the 129th), the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter and note, Ephram's and Vell's letters, both of the broker's papers, Pike's lines on bark, and Oryn's letter on bark. **He has Hesk's brass straightedge, and it reads true in his hand.** He has said "Noted" to Teague three times. He has not answered Ephram.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:885:- **Cael:** nineteen; ten fragments; final deployment **twenty-seven after fixes**; Shadow used exactly twice and sealed; Anchor used twice, once each way; Tide has read Oryn twice in all, each by leave; Cael has read himself three times and has not touched the still place since Oryn's order (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:169-301`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:29-41`). His Hall rib bill goes quiet on day 129 (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:49-51`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:906:- **A7/B9 changed to the final seam:** deployment twenty-seven after fixes; Shadow exactly twice and sealed; the M7 rules remain, with new bills only for contact-set Anchor, Compression ribs, and the permitted Tide reading (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:179-293`; `manuscript/chapter-55.md:155-163,235-301`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md:205:They crossed. Karis's sigil went out at the stride, and she said *gone*, quietly, as she had said it at two other stones. Behind her the healer's lips were moving, and they stopped.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md:209:The path was a stride wide, and it stood a hand above the water. The reeds rose on either side of it higher than Brom's head, dry and rattling, so that they walked in a kind of lane, with a strip of grey sky over them and black water at both elbows. Cael went fourth. He had his ten fragments lying quiet in him, on the far side of a line, and he kept his eyes on Karis's back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-54.md:193:It was the oldest thing that he owned and the quietest, and it had never cost him so much. It went out from under his soles into a foot of moving water and a slab of grey, and what it brought back was dull, and late, like a voice through a wall; he had to lean the whole of his mind upon it to have anything at all. He shut his eyes. There was the plate, and under the plate a hollow, and in the hollow nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-54.md:207:Compression took it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-54.md:213:His ribs told him the price at once, low on the left, in the three places where a mountain had broken them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-54.md:233:A hand had him by the collar, and another under his arm. He was dragged up a face of cut stone like a wet sack, with his ribs shrieking, and laid along the top of it. Seln's voice, close to his ear, said that he was to keep hold of whatever he was holding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-56.md:61:"It's a drover's. It keeps the weight on the ribs and off the joint." The woman did it again. "I've no Path that knits, girl. I can't shut a hole. I can keep one shut for a cold term, if he's the sense to let me, and I've done it for forty of them."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-56.md:117:It kept a road for the first of them, and a grown-over track for the second, and he read the six as he went. The big one was carrying on his left side. The girl was setting her right foot down whole, at every stride, and had been told to. The small one stopped at each halting-place and knelt, and laid something on her knee; and the quiet one, whom he had needed two looks to find in an inn, had been out in front of the rest the whole way, alone. On the third morning the track gave out, and the trail did not so much as waver. That was what he could not get past. People go to water, or to a roof, or along whatever road there is. These had gone over wet grass with no mark to steer by, round nothing, toward nothing that he could see, as a plumb line hangs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:53:The ribs came first, low on the left, the same three, and they hurt a good deal less than they had on a mountain; they were simply *there*, at the top of every breath, like a hand laid on him. Something a great deal heavier than he was had come up under him, and he had sent the whole of it through his own frame into a ledge.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:89:"It's what it always was. There's movement, and I can't count it, and it hasn't a side." She kept her fingers where they were a breath longer than the count wanted. "It's going slower than I ever had it. You've spent something that I can't see. And you're breathing with the top half of you. Which ribs?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:95:"They're not gone again; you'd not have walked that path. They've been leaned on, by a thing that I'd not like to put a weight to." She sat back on her heels. "I can't shut what I can't read. You've heard me say it till you're sick of it. That's ten days of knowing that you've ribs, and they'll talk when it turns cold, and they'll not do more."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:159:*Compression: the strike, standing. The old ribs. Ten days, she says.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-55.md:201:He took his hands from himself, and the going-along came home and lay down. Then he sat up, with his ribs speaking, and wrote by the embers.

