    53	
    54	How many chapters the cold term takes [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19], and which log entries become scenes. The shape of the herd problem and the ice rescue. The content of the silent-yard bouts and who wins each. The texture of the inns, the board room, the ferryman's shed, and the long dark. Letters gone west, with answers pending (none arrive in this movement). Humour: Pike's ledger speech; Brom's "It's a boot"; the mule's shed fee "he has not asked for and will".
    55	
