+3. **Lira's first ask — AMEND PLAN/LEDGER WORDING, KEEP MANUSCRIPT.** Locked Book 7 shows Lira ask Oryn, “Can you mend it?” and “Will you?” on the mountain (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-21.md:165-177`), then states she had asked once (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-21.md:183-185`). Thus “first ask since Norhold” is false (`BOOK_MAP.md:459`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:89`). The draft gives the exact truth: she asked once on the mountain and asked nobody for anything afterward until Thornwater (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:111-115`). Amend plan and ledger to that wording.
+4. **Stroke and bar — AMEND BOOK 8 PLAN, KEEP BOOK 7 AND CURRENT PROSE.** Stake 31 has number/stamp but no stroke-and-bar (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-28.md:119-127`; `chapter-43.md:13`); the newer 32 and unused kit stake 32 have it (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-48.md:203-211`; `chapter-52.md:139-147`); stake 33 has nothing beneath the number (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-53.md:145-153`); and the repeated 34 cordon carries it (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-58.md:165-177`). The current Karis window preserves exactly that distribution (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:161-175`). Amend the future spine claim that the mark is on all four sites; later records may show the grade on survey sheets, but the four field stakes do not.
