+9. **Months — KEEP.** Generic *month* is allowed, no month length is stated, and “Five months and twenty days.” stands verbatim and unglossed (`OWNER-DECISIONS.md:175-180`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:57,235-243`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:83-89`).
+10. **West — RESOLVE AT THE 268TH TABLE.** The 263rd private scene gives the cost and direction without saying the word (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:261-279`). The source's full protected speech begins “It's west” at the six-person table (`books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-01.md:185-189`), so fix 14 makes *west* first spoken on day 268. Amend the plan/packet description of the 263rd from “sentence about west in full” to “costly proposition in full”; the movement then fulfills its promised first utterance, and the day-270 protected log may write it afterward (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:287-289`).
+11. **Sweep probe — NO RULING NEEDED.** The report records that the packet exposed no source range to the author (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:10,124-126`). This audit performed the required protected-only comparison against the historical source and found no unprotected source-shaped passage; only the assigned protected units need restoration.
